719
00:27:52,572 --> 00:27:54,407
- Yes, sir.
But the longer we do nothing,

720
00:27:54,473 --> 00:27:56,042
the harder it is
on the police department.

721
00:27:56,108 --> 00:27:59,012
- People are critical.
We’ve gone through that before.

722
00:27:59,078 --> 00:28:01,782
- The Nardo diamonds have been
missing for three years.

723
00:28:01,848 --> 00:28:03,983
- The Nardo men died
in the electric chair,

724
00:28:04,050 --> 00:28:05,352
and their women are in prison.

725
00:28:05,418 --> 00:28:07,120
- Where the diamonds
are nobody knows.

726
00:28:07,187 --> 00:28:08,588
- Yes.

727
00:28:08,655 --> 00:28:10,590
Probably 'cause
their idea's on empty.

728
00:28:10,657 --> 00:28:12,458
- Seems to me,
we have to find them.

729
00:28:12,525 --> 00:28:13,760
- Duh!

730
00:28:13,827 --> 00:28:15,528
- Lee, you're probably
the finest police woman

731
00:28:15,595 --> 00:28:16,562
I’ve ever known.

732
00:28:16,628 --> 00:28:17,797
- Oh, pshaw!

733
00:28:17,863 --> 00:28:20,200
- You’re right,
and your plan’s right.

734
00:28:20,267 --> 00:28:21,968
Josie Nardo
and those other girls

735
00:28:22,035 --> 00:28:23,837
are bound to know
where the diamonds are.

736
00:28:23,903 --> 00:28:25,205
- Of course, they do.

737
00:28:25,272 --> 00:28:27,040
- So if we put you in prison,

738
00:28:27,140 --> 00:28:28,140
you escape
with the Nardo girls,

739
00:28:28,207 --> 00:28:29,908
you’ll know
where the diamonds are.

740
00:28:29,975 --> 00:28:31,945
I think you’ll stick around
and tell us what you find out.

741
00:28:32,012 --> 00:28:33,413
- You flatter me, sir.

742
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:35,215
- What do you think you ought to
send me to jail for?

743
00:28:35,282 --> 00:28:36,282
- Bravery.

744
00:28:36,348 --> 00:28:39,085
- And sweet love
beyond the call of duty.

745
00:28:39,152 --> 00:28:41,487
- But, sir,
what does this have to do

746
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:42,922
with the whole
Touch Conners thing?

747
00:28:42,988 --> 00:28:45,592
- ...with the Nardo girls
on the second floor.

748
00:28:45,658 --> 00:28:47,460
- Any electric alarms
on the windows?

749
00:28:47,527 --> 00:28:48,695
- No.
- That's extra.

750
00:28:48,762 --> 00:28:51,998
- The fence is here
in a direct line.

751
00:28:52,065 --> 00:28:53,900
- ♪ Lovely Rita meter maid ♪

752
00:28:53,967 --> 00:28:55,335
- Car right here
in front of the trees.

753
00:28:55,402 --> 00:28:56,435
- Every night?
- Every night.

754
00:28:56,502 --> 00:28:58,505
You pick your
own time of departure.

755
00:28:58,572 --> 00:29:00,072
- Sooner the better.

756
00:29:00,140 --> 00:29:01,875
- There's got to be shooting,
Lee. We'll miss.

757
00:29:01,942 --> 00:29:03,510
- I hope so.

758
00:29:03,577 --> 00:29:06,312
- And you’ve got to be pursued,
unsuccessfully, of course.

759
00:29:06,378 --> 00:29:08,748
- Story of my life, sir.

760
00:29:08,815 --> 00:29:10,517
- I'll give you
all the protection I can,

761
00:29:10,583 --> 00:29:12,252
but we’ve got to be careful.

762
00:29:12,318 --> 00:29:14,053
The slightest suspicion,
they’ll kill you.

763
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:15,222
- Yes, sir.

764
00:29:15,288 --> 00:29:17,223
- Well, can I drive
you to jail?

765
00:29:17,290 --> 00:29:18,492
- Sergeant Morrison
will take you

766
00:29:18,558 --> 00:29:19,658
to the prison tomorrow morning.

767
00:29:19,725 --> 00:29:20,693
- Thank you, sir.

768
00:29:20,760 --> 00:29:21,962
- And I have to get back
to my ship.

769
00:29:22,028 --> 00:29:23,763
- You’re taking
on a mighty big job, Lee.

770
00:29:23,830 --> 00:29:28,233
- I guess I can't resist
my share of the diamonds, huh?

771
00:29:28,300 --> 00:29:30,102
- Good luck. Good-bye.

772
00:29:30,203 --> 00:29:31,237
- Good-bye, sir.

773
00:29:32,372 --> 00:29:34,540
- So no kiss, huh?

774
00:29:34,607 --> 00:29:36,742
- Hey, looks
like a Catholic grade school.

775
00:29:36,810 --> 00:29:40,012
- Our Lady of French Guiana
from which there is no escape.

776
00:29:41,948 --> 00:29:43,483
- [ speaks French ]

777
00:29:43,550 --> 00:29:44,617
- Will you get
out of my way,

778
00:29:44,683 --> 00:29:46,385
or do I have to beat
you out of here?

779
00:29:46,452 --> 00:29:47,953
- Yeah, Beverly, go get her!

780
00:29:48,020 --> 00:29:49,222
- Aw, leave her alone.

781
00:29:49,288 --> 00:29:50,257
- Stay out of this!

782
00:29:50,323 --> 00:29:51,790
- Leave her alone!

783
00:29:51,858 --> 00:29:53,325
- She got in my way!

784
00:29:53,392 --> 00:29:56,095
- Want to knock somebody around,
try your own size.

785
00:29:56,162 --> 00:29:57,830
- Like who?
- Me.

786
00:29:57,897 --> 00:29:59,798
- Hey, that does make
a lot more sense.

787
00:29:59,865 --> 00:30:01,033
- Why don’t you shut up?

788
00:30:01,100 --> 00:30:04,203
- It’s Lucy and Viv
in the big house.

789
00:30:04,270 --> 00:30:06,072
- Welcome to Dye Job Theater.

790
00:30:07,873 --> 00:30:10,343
- Well, if you two ain’t
a sight for sore eyes.

791
00:30:10,410 --> 00:30:12,212
- They’re all doing
a nickel at UPS.

792
00:30:12,278 --> 00:30:14,680
- I don’t know about your eyes,
but I sure got a sore back.

793
00:30:14,747 --> 00:30:15,682
- Not from working.

794
00:30:15,748 --> 00:30:16,715
- Whoa!

795
00:30:16,782 --> 00:30:18,250
- What's up, Josie?

796
00:30:18,317 --> 00:30:19,652
- I just thought
I'd drop around.

797
00:30:19,718 --> 00:30:22,088
- Get yourself put in the brig
for being down here.

798
00:30:22,155 --> 00:30:24,323
- They made me a trustee.

799
00:30:24,390 --> 00:30:25,558
- Huh!

800
00:30:25,625 --> 00:30:26,558
- Typical.

801
00:30:26,625 --> 00:30:27,560
- I got a new roommate.

802
00:30:27,627 --> 00:30:28,895
- Name's Leona.

803
00:30:28,962 --> 00:30:30,763
- They sure like to make trouble
for us, don’t they?

804
00:30:30,830 --> 00:30:32,598
- She’s crazier than a bedbug.

805
00:30:32,665 --> 00:30:33,867
- How can you tell?

806
00:30:33,967 --> 00:30:35,468
- She’s only
been here three hours.

807
00:30:35,535 --> 00:30:36,870
She wants to go
over the wall.

808
00:30:36,937 --> 00:30:39,172
- Huh. Don’t sound
so crazy to me.

809
00:30:39,238 --> 00:30:40,640
- Well, we let
her go over the wall,

810
00:30:40,707 --> 00:30:41,942
they shoot her,
and we’re...

811
00:30:42,008 --> 00:30:44,010
- Oh, yes, that's what
we'll end up doing.

812
00:30:44,077 --> 00:30:46,512
- [ speaking indistinctly ]

813
00:30:46,578 --> 00:30:47,680
- Huh?

814
00:30:47,747 --> 00:30:50,048
- Guys, it’s
a prison slumber party.

815
00:30:50,115 --> 00:30:51,717
- Yeah, they use razors
in the pillows

816
00:30:51,783 --> 00:30:52,885
for the pillow fights.

817
00:30:54,487 --> 00:30:57,057
- Okay, I’m a cop.
Don't hurt me.

818
00:30:57,123 --> 00:30:58,892
- When moms go bad.

819
00:30:58,958 --> 00:31:01,127
- Move it.
- Shut up.

820
00:31:01,193 --> 00:31:03,162
- Oh, both of you shut up.

821
00:31:03,228 --> 00:31:04,663
- They’re all strung out
on Correctol.

822
00:31:04,730 --> 00:31:06,732
- Don’t you know we’re very hard
to get along with?

823
00:31:06,765 --> 00:31:08,500
- Well, I wasn’t thinking
of have a pleasure trip.

824
00:31:08,568 --> 00:31:11,503
- Oh, what were you
thinking of, suicide?

825
00:31:11,570 --> 00:31:13,172
- No, you have to guess.

826
00:31:13,238 --> 00:31:14,840
- The Nardo diamonds.

827
00:31:14,907 --> 00:31:16,943
- Wouldn’t you just like to get
your hands on them?

828
00:31:17,010 --> 00:31:18,343
- Wouldn’t you?

829
00:31:18,410 --> 00:31:21,013
- Look, we’ve been in here
for three lousy years.

830
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:23,583
What makes you think right away
you can crash this joint?

831
00:31:23,650 --> 00:31:26,118
- Well, I did something
you three girls didn’t do.

832
00:31:26,185 --> 00:31:27,553
- She was deloused.

833
00:31:27,620 --> 00:31:29,588
- Man, I didn’t think
we missed nothing.

834
00:31:29,655 --> 00:31:31,090
- Such as what?

835
00:31:31,157 --> 00:31:33,525
- On my way in,
I planned a way out.

836
00:31:33,593 --> 00:31:35,728
- Oh, we should have done that.

837
00:31:35,795 --> 00:31:37,097
[ bell rings ]

838
00:31:37,130 --> 00:31:38,397
- Which twin has the Toni?

839
00:31:40,733 --> 00:31:43,102
- Cool it, the RA’s coming!

840
00:31:43,168 --> 00:31:45,338
- A prison filled
with Wendy Darlings.

841
00:31:47,007 --> 00:31:48,540
- Bring me that case of tea.

842
00:31:48,608 --> 00:31:51,410
- And the head
of Alfredo Garcia.

843
00:31:51,477 --> 00:31:53,747
- A true story of Land’s End.

844
00:31:55,615 --> 00:31:57,917
- What makes you so sure
we’ll split with you?

845
00:31:57,983 --> 00:32:00,018
- What makes you sure
that I’ll take you with me?

846
00:32:00,085 --> 00:32:02,488
- Anyway, be quiet
about our secret plan!

847
00:32:02,555 --> 00:32:03,690
- She’ll be there.

848
00:32:03,757 --> 00:32:05,057
- Who’s putting it there?

849
00:32:05,123 --> 00:32:06,192
- None of your business.

850
00:32:06,258 --> 00:32:07,327
- Well, who else will be there?

851
00:32:07,393 --> 00:32:10,630
Can I bring Susan
from cellblock 8?

852
00:32:10,697 --> 00:32:12,932
- Boy,
she sure thinks she’s hot.

853
00:32:12,998 --> 00:32:16,035
- I think she is, too,
if she can get us out of here.

854
00:32:16,102 --> 00:32:18,503
- Sales have gone up
since she’s been here.

855
00:32:18,570 --> 00:32:21,140
- Back now
to Vinyl Window Theater.

856
00:32:22,575 --> 00:32:25,512
- See? They come apart,
but keep it a secret!

857
00:32:25,578 --> 00:32:27,413
- We’ve been doing
a little planning, too.

858
00:32:27,480 --> 00:32:29,115
- It’s a long drop.

859
00:32:29,182 --> 00:32:30,783
- What’s the matter?
No guts?

860
00:32:30,850 --> 00:32:32,152
- Takes more than guts.

861
00:32:32,218 --> 00:32:33,753
- Still, it does take guts.

862
00:32:33,820 --> 00:32:34,853
- We need your car.

863
00:32:34,920 --> 00:32:36,822
- How much
are the diamonds worth?

864
00:32:36,888 --> 00:32:39,625
- Any fence
will give us 200 grand.

865
00:32:39,692 --> 00:32:41,093
- Can you find them?

866
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:43,095
- I can find them.

867
00:32:43,162 --> 00:32:44,463
- I get 50 grand.

868
00:32:44,530 --> 00:32:46,665
- Yeah, 50 grand.

869
00:32:46,732 --> 00:32:48,935
- So, if you ever have to leave,
that’s how you do it.

870
00:32:49,002 --> 00:32:50,870
- We get there...
- And back.

871
00:32:52,572 --> 00:32:54,473
- It's morning in Joliet.

872
00:32:54,540 --> 00:32:56,608
[ imitating birds whistling ]

873
00:32:56,675 --> 00:32:58,143
- I can hardly sleep.
How about you?

874
00:32:58,210 --> 00:33:00,680
I’m so excited.

875
00:33:00,747 --> 00:33:03,215
We’re going to be the first ones
in line for the scrambled eggs!

876
00:33:03,282 --> 00:33:04,417
- Hooray!

877
00:33:06,485 --> 00:33:08,153
- Wait a minute,
it worked yesterday.

878
00:33:08,220 --> 00:33:09,522
I don’t know what happened.

879
00:33:09,588 --> 00:33:11,523
- Well, it was loose,
so I welded it back.

880
00:33:13,558 --> 00:33:15,395
- These women
are actually escaping

881
00:33:15,462 --> 00:33:17,730
in Easy Spirit dress pumps.

882
00:33:17,797 --> 00:33:19,165
- [ imitating Colonel Klink ]
No one has ever escaped

883
00:33:19,232 --> 00:33:20,700
from Stalag 13!

884
00:33:20,767 --> 00:33:22,235
- Of course not.

885
00:33:23,302 --> 00:33:25,037
- Tell me, boy,
what day is it?

886
00:33:25,103 --> 00:33:27,673
- It’s Christmas day, sir.

887
00:33:27,740 --> 00:33:29,908
- What’s with
the Get Smart music?

888
00:33:32,345 --> 00:33:33,913
- Okay, let’s go.

889
00:33:33,980 --> 00:33:36,148
Aaah!

890
00:33:39,518 --> 00:33:41,720
Aah!

891
00:33:41,787 --> 00:33:44,657
- Don’t forget to bring me
a Dove Bar!

892
00:33:46,992 --> 00:33:49,895
- This is riveting.
- Mm-hmm.

893
00:33:49,962 --> 00:33:52,698
- Bombs away!

894
00:33:55,367 --> 00:33:56,668
- Wait, we can’t leave.

895
00:33:56,735 --> 00:33:58,905
They’re having
creamed corn today.

896
00:34:01,573 --> 00:34:03,275
- Why am I thinking
of Joe Theismann?

897
00:34:03,342 --> 00:34:05,545
[ alarm bells ringing ]

898
00:34:08,180 --> 00:34:09,848
- I hit the bell on my way out!

899
00:34:09,915 --> 00:34:11,117
I hope that’s okay!

900
00:34:11,183 --> 00:34:13,252
[ sirens ]

901
00:34:13,318 --> 00:34:17,423
- [ shouting German-accented
gibberish ]

902
00:34:18,723 --> 00:34:20,793
- Sounds like the Foley artists
are chasing us!

903
00:34:20,860 --> 00:34:22,395
Let’s hit it!

904
00:34:22,462 --> 00:34:24,597
- The Kids in the Hall escaped
from prison!

905
00:34:28,200 --> 00:34:30,402
- [ shouting
Russian-accented gibberish ]

906
00:34:34,740 --> 00:34:36,775
Schnell!

907
00:34:36,842 --> 00:34:39,745
- Hey, let’s take this one.
This one's nice.

908
00:34:39,812 --> 00:34:43,115
- This car
is so convenient.

909
00:34:43,182 --> 00:34:44,950
- Oh, and it’s so roomy.
This is a nice car.

910
00:34:45,017 --> 00:34:46,652
- Ooh, and so clean.

911
00:34:46,718 --> 00:34:48,053
- Floor mats and everything.

912
00:34:48,120 --> 00:34:49,488
It's got that new car smell.

913
00:34:49,522 --> 00:34:51,723
- ♪ Oh-ho,
the Wells Fargo wagon-- ♪

914
00:34:51,790 --> 00:34:53,192
- [ police sirens ]
- Look out!

915
00:34:53,258 --> 00:34:54,393
[ gunshots ]

916
00:34:54,460 --> 00:34:56,228
- Boy, I sure do wish
I had a gun.

917
00:34:56,295 --> 00:34:57,630
- Ow! Take it easy!

918
00:34:57,697 --> 00:34:59,098
- What’s the matter?

919
00:34:59,165 --> 00:35:01,567
- Watch my arm, that's what.
- Oh, that's tough.

920
00:35:01,633 --> 00:35:03,135
- Watch that turn.

921
00:35:03,202 --> 00:35:04,270
- That one?

922
00:35:05,838 --> 00:35:07,707
- Ladies, it’s a big car.
You can spread out a little.

923
00:35:07,773 --> 00:35:09,308
- Where do we go from here?
- We're losing them!

924
00:35:09,375 --> 00:35:10,943
- Turn left half a mile up.

925
00:35:11,010 --> 00:35:12,245
- I’m up
for something chickeny.

926
00:35:12,312 --> 00:35:14,913
- Louie Blanc?
- Yeah.

927
00:35:14,980 --> 00:35:16,748
- Hey, you think he'll give us
something decent

928
00:35:16,815 --> 00:35:18,217
to wear and some lipstick?

929
00:35:18,283 --> 00:35:20,052
- Good enough
for where we’re going.

930
00:35:20,118 --> 00:35:21,287
- They've given up.

931
00:35:21,320 --> 00:35:22,588
Boy, I sure do wish

932
00:35:22,655 --> 00:35:23,923
I could have taken
a couple shots at them.

933
00:35:23,990 --> 00:35:25,290
- Hey, and a couple of shots,
a couple of shots...

934
00:35:25,357 --> 00:35:26,625
[ speaking like auctioneer ]

935
00:35:26,692 --> 00:35:28,460
- He will if he knows
what’s good for him.

936
00:35:28,527 --> 00:35:30,262
- How long do you think
it’s going to take us, Josie?

937
00:35:30,328 --> 00:35:32,565
- Oh, took a couple of days
with the boys.

938
00:35:32,632 --> 00:35:34,233
I don’t see how
we can do much better.

939
00:35:34,300 --> 00:35:35,233
- On foot?

940
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:36,468
- In these shoes?

941
00:35:36,535 --> 00:35:38,537
- On foot, it’d take
about a couple of years.

942
00:35:38,603 --> 00:35:41,040
- Louie will give us a boat.

943
00:35:41,107 --> 00:35:42,975
We got a few things
on Louie.

944
00:35:43,042 --> 00:35:45,778
- Yeah, we saw him coming out
of Lend Me a Tenor.

945
00:35:45,845 --> 00:35:47,913
[ tires squealing ]

946
00:35:47,980 --> 00:35:49,215
- I’m spritzing.

947
00:35:49,282 --> 00:35:51,217
Any of you mugs
got a problem with that?

948
00:35:51,283 --> 00:35:52,985
- What’s on your mind?

949
00:35:53,052 --> 00:35:54,187
- Nobody has any guns yet.

950
00:35:54,220 --> 00:35:55,487
- [ doing auctioneer call ]

951
00:35:55,555 --> 00:35:57,423
- If it weren't for me,
you'd all rot in jail.

952
00:35:57,490 --> 00:35:59,525
I want to make sure
I get that 50 grand.

953
00:35:59,592 --> 00:36:01,293
- We keep bargains.

954
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:03,628
- I just thought I’d tell you.

955
00:36:03,695 --> 00:36:05,063
- Hi.

956
00:36:05,130 --> 00:36:06,498
- I’m a good shot.

957
00:36:06,565 --> 00:36:08,467
If you try anything,
I’ll kill all three of you.

958
00:36:08,533 --> 00:36:09,735
- And if you try something...

959
00:36:09,802 --> 00:36:11,003
- We’ll kill you.

960
00:36:11,070 --> 00:36:12,772
- Well, I guess
I had that coming.

961
00:36:12,838 --> 00:36:14,640
- Now that we’ve bonded
let’s go.

962
00:36:17,108 --> 00:36:19,645
- Well, this is going
to be fun. Oh!

963
00:36:25,317 --> 00:36:26,418
- Honey.

964
00:36:26,518 --> 00:36:27,587
- Shut up, Iris.

965
00:36:27,653 --> 00:36:28,820
- It’s lovely.

966
00:36:28,888 --> 00:36:30,690
- Yeah, it’s great, isn’t it?

967
00:36:30,757 --> 00:36:32,692
- Just lovely.

968
00:36:32,758 --> 00:36:35,762
- Yeah, I’m going to dredge it
and put up condos.

969
00:36:35,828 --> 00:36:37,597
- But then, of course,

970
00:36:37,663 --> 00:36:39,965
after you got
a few little ol' oil wells,

971
00:36:40,032 --> 00:36:42,268
you wouldn’t have to spend
any time in a nasty jungle.

972
00:36:42,335 --> 00:36:43,368
- Uh, what’s that?
Hold on.

973
00:36:43,435 --> 00:36:45,572
I got a big wax ball up here.
There.

974
00:36:45,638 --> 00:36:47,240
- No, I guess not.

975
00:36:47,307 --> 00:36:51,010
- Nice little scene.

976
00:36:51,077 --> 00:36:52,812
Oh, the two plots are
on a collision course.

977
00:36:52,878 --> 00:36:54,913
- Really a great time
to spring a leak.

978
00:36:54,980 --> 00:36:57,850
- If I ever see that lousy Louie
again, I’ll break his neck.

979
00:36:57,883 --> 00:36:59,585
- Josie, what do we do now?

980
00:36:59,652 --> 00:37:01,353
- Hitch a ride, I guess.

981
00:37:01,420 --> 00:37:03,222
- Hey, wait a minute.

982
00:37:03,288 --> 00:37:05,958
- We don’t have to do anything!

983
00:37:06,025 --> 00:37:07,693
Here comes Touch Conners!

984
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:09,095
- Oh.

985
00:37:09,162 --> 00:37:10,630
- Hey, look over there.

986
00:37:10,697 --> 00:37:12,665
- Young girls
in primary colors.

987
00:37:15,533 --> 00:37:16,802
- Come on over here!

988
00:37:18,303 --> 00:37:20,773
- Get over here! We just want
to kill you for a minute!

989
00:37:20,840 --> 00:37:21,940
- Yeah.
- Okay.

990
00:37:22,007 --> 00:37:23,075
- Come on!

991
00:37:25,878 --> 00:37:27,245
- Cut it, I said.

992
00:37:27,313 --> 00:37:29,382
- Let go of the boat.
- What's your problem, girls?

993
00:37:29,482 --> 00:37:31,517
- Bob, honey, I'm frightened
What do they want?

994
00:37:31,583 --> 00:37:33,652
- Just the boat.
Pull it into shore.

995
00:37:33,718 --> 00:37:35,553
- Now, wait a minute.
What do you think this is?

996
00:37:35,622 --> 00:37:37,657
- Uncle Charlie, no!
- [ gunshot ]

997
00:37:37,723 --> 00:37:40,827
- Steve, Chip, Ernie!
[ blubbing ]

998
00:37:44,097 --> 00:37:45,330
- Oh!

999
00:37:45,397 --> 00:37:47,333
- What’s the matter with you?
Are you crazy?

1000
00:37:49,135 --> 00:37:50,737
- ♪ Da dun da dun ♪
Save yourself!

1001
00:37:50,803 --> 00:37:53,738
- You’re no Mannix
to me, mister!

1002
00:37:53,805 --> 00:37:56,542
- Oh, I’m binding.
Can't you tell I'm binding?

1003
00:37:56,608 --> 00:38:00,947
- Oh, man, he landed
right on the wax worms.

1004
00:38:01,013 --> 00:38:03,548
- Um, sorry
about Mr. Demarest.

1005
00:38:03,615 --> 00:38:05,250
- You were in prison?

1006
00:38:05,317 --> 00:38:06,652
Do you know Bubba?

1007
00:38:06,718 --> 00:38:08,087
- What’s this?

1008
00:38:08,153 --> 00:38:09,488
Touch Conners is being helped
from the field,

1009
00:38:09,555 --> 00:38:11,557
but he should return
in the second half.

1010
00:38:11,623 --> 00:38:12,825
[ imitating crowd cheering ]

1011
00:38:12,892 --> 00:38:14,360
- Splashing water all over me!

1012
00:38:19,632 --> 00:38:22,033
- Ow, ow, ow, ow!

1013
00:38:22,100 --> 00:38:24,870
Ow, owie, oh!

1014
00:38:24,937 --> 00:38:26,072
- What’s your dream?

1015
00:38:28,440 --> 00:38:30,175
- It’s love!

1016
00:38:30,242 --> 00:38:31,843
- What’s the matter?

1017
00:38:31,910 --> 00:38:34,047
- Oh, my fantasy!

1018
00:38:34,113 --> 00:38:36,115
Oh. Nope,
she can’t take it there.

1019
00:38:36,182 --> 00:38:38,117
She can’t take it there.

1020
00:38:41,553 --> 00:38:43,255
- Come on, break it up!

1021
00:38:43,322 --> 00:38:44,790
- We’ve got guests!

1022
00:38:44,857 --> 00:38:46,658
- What’s the matter?

1023
00:38:46,725 --> 00:38:49,195
- That guy tried to conk me
over the head with an oar,

1024
00:38:49,262 --> 00:38:50,730
and I shot him,
and she jumped me!

1025
00:38:50,797 --> 00:38:52,097
- Now, hold it.

1026
00:38:52,163 --> 00:38:54,467
- You both came to see me.
That's the first step.

1027
00:38:54,533 --> 00:38:55,567
- There shouldn’t be
any shooting.

1028
00:38:55,633 --> 00:38:56,635
- What’s the matter,
you chicken?

1029
00:38:56,702 --> 00:38:57,903
- In case you want to know,

1030
00:38:57,970 --> 00:38:59,872
shots make noise,
and noise carries.

1031
00:38:59,938 --> 00:39:01,207
- Ooh.

1032
00:39:01,273 --> 00:39:02,240
- There's no reason
why we should attract

1033
00:39:02,307 --> 00:39:03,308
any more attention
than we have to.

1034
00:39:03,375 --> 00:39:05,277
- Says who?
- She's got a point.

1035
00:39:05,377 --> 00:39:06,812
Now quit the fighting.

1036
00:39:06,878 --> 00:39:08,080
Give her back her gun.

1037
00:39:08,147 --> 00:39:09,148
- Who wants guns?

1038
00:39:09,215 --> 00:39:10,348
- I do, I do!

1039
00:39:10,415 --> 00:39:11,817
- No hard feelings.

1040
00:39:11,883 --> 00:39:13,218
- That's what you think.

1041
00:39:13,285 --> 00:39:14,487
- That’s what I think.

1042
00:39:14,553 --> 00:39:15,653
- Do you like Elly Mae?

1043
00:39:15,722 --> 00:39:17,990
- You all right?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

1044
00:39:18,057 --> 00:39:20,292
- Ow...ow...owie.

1045
00:39:20,358 --> 00:39:21,793
Ohh.

1046
00:39:21,860 --> 00:39:23,328
- Hello, breakfast.

1047
00:39:25,097 --> 00:39:28,533
- Well, we caught it,
but what is it?

1048
00:39:28,600 --> 00:39:29,968
- You could have killed him.

1049
00:39:30,035 --> 00:39:31,337
- Well, we didn’t, did we?

1050
00:39:31,403 --> 00:39:32,472
- Oh, we should have.

1051
00:39:32,538 --> 00:39:34,073
- I didn’t see much else
we can do.

1052
00:39:34,140 --> 00:39:35,540
- Oh, just wait
till he wakes up.

1053
00:39:35,607 --> 00:39:36,808
He won’t know what hit him.

1054
00:39:36,842 --> 00:39:37,877
- But what’s the pelt worth?

1055
00:39:37,943 --> 00:39:39,545
- Maybe I better not.
- Oh, hold it.

1056
00:39:39,612 --> 00:39:40,678
- Will you let me alone?

1057
00:39:40,747 --> 00:39:41,880
- You’re crazy for that gun.

1058
00:39:41,947 --> 00:39:43,148
- Knock it off.

1059
00:39:43,215 --> 00:39:44,850
- She just wants to kill
somebody, doesn't she?

1060
00:39:44,917 --> 00:39:46,052
- Mm-hmm.

1061
00:39:46,118 --> 00:39:47,753
- Yeah, hold them both
as hostages.

1062
00:39:47,820 --> 00:39:48,920
- Have you held
your hostage today?

1063
00:39:48,987 --> 00:39:50,088
- We got a long trip
ahead of us.

1064
00:39:50,155 --> 00:39:51,590
We might run into trouble.

1065
00:39:51,657 --> 00:39:54,058
I’d like something to bargain
with, and they'd do.

1066
00:39:54,127 --> 00:39:55,928
- Diamonds and guns ain’t enough
of a bargain?

1067
00:39:55,995 --> 00:39:57,530
- ♪ Diamonds and guns ♪

1068
00:39:57,597 --> 00:39:59,765
- Oh, get it yourself.

1069
00:39:59,832 --> 00:40:01,300
- She’s right.
We better tie him up.

1070
00:40:01,367 --> 00:40:02,735
Go on, hurry there.

1071
00:40:04,737 --> 00:40:07,205
- I got a little poem.

1072
00:40:07,272 --> 00:40:08,340
- Kind of go for him.

1073
00:40:08,440 --> 00:40:11,043
- Nice enough looking.

1074
00:40:11,110 --> 00:40:12,110
- Stupid name, though.

1075
00:40:13,578 --> 00:40:16,115
- I call it the mid-section.

1076
00:40:16,182 --> 00:40:17,950
- Wonder who he is?

1077
00:40:18,017 --> 00:40:19,752
- Poor little guy.
I think he's lost.

1078
00:40:19,818 --> 00:40:21,353
- Couldn’t be a friend of yours,
could he?

1079
00:40:21,420 --> 00:40:24,223
- You know, I got a feeling you
don’t like me.

1080
00:40:24,290 --> 00:40:27,392
- Hey, I’m not dreaming.

1081
00:40:27,460 --> 00:40:28,793
- You okay?

1082
00:40:28,860 --> 00:40:29,862
- I guess so.

1083
00:40:29,928 --> 00:40:31,297
What’s the story?

1084
00:40:31,363 --> 00:40:33,132
- Enchanted April
meets Deliverance.

1085
00:40:33,198 --> 00:40:35,633
- Man, don’t you read
the papers?

1086
00:40:35,700 --> 00:40:37,068
- Once in a while.

1087
00:40:37,135 --> 00:40:38,403
- Ever heard
of the Nardo gang?

1088
00:40:38,470 --> 00:40:41,407
- Yeah. Said they’re
a pretty rough group.

1089
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:42,575
- You just remember that.

1090
00:40:42,642 --> 00:40:43,575
- Oh, thank you very much!

1091
00:40:43,642 --> 00:40:44,943
- Okay, Red.

1092
00:40:45,010 --> 00:40:48,147
- Oh, Bob, honey.
What are they going to do?

1093
00:40:48,213 --> 00:40:49,148
- Shut up.

1094
00:40:49,215 --> 00:40:50,448
- Thanks, White.

1095
00:40:50,515 --> 00:40:51,450
- She's got a good question.
- [ woman crying ]

1096
00:40:51,517 --> 00:40:52,852
What are you going to do?

1097
00:40:52,918 --> 00:40:55,287
- Stick around,
then you’ll know, too.

1098
00:40:55,353 --> 00:40:56,288
- Ooh.

1099
00:40:56,355 --> 00:40:57,590
- Kidnapping maybe?

1100
00:40:57,657 --> 00:40:58,957
- If you’re lucky.

1101
00:40:59,023 --> 00:41:00,525
- What’s your name?

1102
00:41:00,592 --> 00:41:01,727
- Bob.

1103
00:41:01,793 --> 00:41:02,928
- Okay, it's Fred!

1104
00:41:02,995 --> 00:41:04,230
- Bob Matthews.

1105
00:41:04,297 --> 00:41:06,232
Not worth much
in this kidnapping game.

1106
00:41:06,298 --> 00:41:08,400
- Yeah, that’s
very discouraging.

1107
00:41:08,467 --> 00:41:10,135
That your wife?

1108
00:41:10,202 --> 00:41:11,203
- No.

1109
00:41:11,270 --> 00:41:12,303
- No, no, no, no.

1110
00:41:12,370 --> 00:41:13,372
- A friend.

1111
00:41:13,438 --> 00:41:15,673
- Some friend.

1112
00:41:15,740 --> 00:41:17,408
- Look, if you don't stop
your crying,

1113
00:41:17,475 --> 00:41:18,743
I’ll give you something
to cry about.

1114
00:41:18,810 --> 00:41:20,145
- My dad used to say that.

1115
00:41:20,212 --> 00:41:21,980
- Yeah, one more girl
we don’t need.

1116
00:41:22,047 --> 00:41:23,048
- What can I do for you?

1117
00:41:23,115 --> 00:41:24,850
- Can you get us
Peggy’s autograph?

1118
00:41:24,917 --> 00:41:26,318
- We had a leaky boat
with no motor.

1119
00:41:26,385 --> 00:41:27,920
Anyway,
we like yours better.

1120
00:41:27,987 --> 00:41:30,122
- So you’re off
on a cruise, huh?

1121
00:41:30,188 --> 00:41:31,190
- Yeah.

1122
00:41:31,257 --> 00:41:32,457
- Sounds fun.

1123
00:41:32,525 --> 00:41:33,892
- Why’d you have
to kill the guide?

1124
00:41:33,958 --> 00:41:34,893
- For effect.

1125
00:41:34,960 --> 00:41:36,228
- Self-defense.

1126
00:41:36,295 --> 00:41:38,563
- Er...I had one other thing
I was going to ask.

1127
00:41:38,630 --> 00:41:39,965
- Well, come on.
Let's get going.

1128
00:41:40,032 --> 00:41:42,033
- Okay.

1129
00:41:42,100 --> 00:41:44,503
[ grunts ]
♪ Da dum da dum da dum ♪

1130
00:41:47,673 --> 00:41:50,175
- Head upstream,
keep her down the middle.

1131
00:41:50,242 --> 00:41:51,443
- Okay.
And what would you say

1132
00:41:51,510 --> 00:41:53,512
is the load limit
for this thing?

1133
00:41:53,578 --> 00:41:55,882
- Listen, we got to have
this boat back in an hour.

1134
00:41:55,948 --> 00:41:57,550
I left my license.

1135
00:42:00,185 --> 00:42:01,753
- Do you guys think
it's possible

1136
00:42:01,820 --> 00:42:03,388
that the Video Watchdog people
are wrong

1137
00:42:03,455 --> 00:42:05,590
and that Corman really is
a terrible director?

1138
00:42:05,657 --> 00:42:07,525
- [ screams ]
- God, you scared me!

1139
00:42:07,593 --> 00:42:08,793
- What is that?

1140
00:42:08,860 --> 00:42:10,862
- Oh, sit down.
It's just an alligator.

1141
00:42:10,930 --> 00:42:12,530
- Just an alligator?

1142
00:42:12,598 --> 00:42:14,933
- Boy, we’re having more fun
than I thought!

1143
00:42:16,502 --> 00:42:19,938
- GAF View-Master
presents the Okefenokee.

1144
00:42:20,005 --> 00:42:22,942
- I think they’re headed
for Doug Kershaw’s place.

1145
00:42:25,912 --> 00:42:29,515
- ♪ Spanish moss,
the land of the Chia ♪

1146
00:42:29,582 --> 00:42:32,050
- I wonder what other names
Touch Conners considered

1147
00:42:32,117 --> 00:42:33,618
before he hit on Touch?

1148
00:42:33,685 --> 00:42:34,820
- Thrust?
- Jab?

1149
00:42:34,887 --> 00:42:36,455
- Punch
- Crunch?

1150
00:42:36,522 --> 00:42:38,023
- Splat.
- Smidge.

1151
00:42:38,090 --> 00:42:39,090
- Shout.
- Batch.

1152
00:42:39,157 --> 00:42:40,092
- Um, Scrub.

1153
00:42:40,158 --> 00:42:41,127
- Flake.
- Wink.

1154
00:42:41,193 --> 00:42:43,595
- Sploot?

1155
00:42:43,662 --> 00:42:46,098
- Josie, how much further
we got to go?

1156
00:42:46,165 --> 00:42:48,633
- Just till we find
a dry spot to land.

1157
00:42:48,733 --> 00:42:49,835
- Hey, look at that!

1158
00:42:49,902 --> 00:42:50,970
[ birds squawking ]

1159
00:42:51,037 --> 00:42:52,503
- Ah, Uganda.

1160
00:42:54,773 --> 00:42:57,408
- Hey, you son of a gun,
gonna have big fun.

1161
00:42:57,475 --> 00:42:59,143
- Bob, what's happening?

1162
00:42:59,210 --> 00:43:01,947
- Not much,
how about with you?

1163
00:43:02,013 --> 00:43:04,015
- Well, my chest
has fallen asleep.

1164
00:43:04,082 --> 00:43:05,217
- Don’t worry, honey.

1165
00:43:05,283 --> 00:43:06,418
It'll be all right.

1166
00:43:06,485 --> 00:43:08,787
- That’s very sweet.

1167
00:43:08,853 --> 00:43:10,788
- Sure, you can use it.

1168
00:43:10,855 --> 00:43:12,792
- Red, you talk too much.

1169
00:43:13,858 --> 00:43:16,895
Oh, cut it out.

1170
00:43:16,962 --> 00:43:18,797
- Beverly can sure handle
a Johnson, can’t she?

1171
00:43:18,863 --> 00:43:20,465
- Yes, she can.
- Mm-hmm.

1172
00:43:20,498 --> 00:43:21,967
- That looks like dry ground.

1173
00:43:22,033 --> 00:43:23,768
We can camp over there.

1174
00:43:23,835 --> 00:43:26,605
- It sure ain’t no palace.

1175
00:43:26,672 --> 00:43:28,207
- It ain’t no prison,
either.

1176
00:43:28,273 --> 00:43:29,675
- It’s sort of in the middle.

1177
00:43:29,742 --> 00:43:31,177
- Get out and pull the boat in.

1178
00:43:31,243 --> 00:43:33,145
- "Billie, do this,
Billie, do that."

1179
00:43:33,212 --> 00:43:34,480
- You heard me.

1180
00:43:34,547 --> 00:43:38,817
- And remember, try not to kill
anyone this time.

1181
00:43:40,652 --> 00:43:42,520
- Pinch Conners?

1182
00:43:42,587 --> 00:43:43,655
- Probe Conners.

1183
00:43:43,722 --> 00:43:45,090
- Hmm.
- Wing Conners?

1184
00:43:45,157 --> 00:43:46,525
- Hmm, Mike.

1185
00:43:46,592 --> 00:43:47,960
- Are you complaining?

1186
00:43:48,027 --> 00:43:49,628
- Man, you know I am.

1187
00:43:56,035 --> 00:43:57,635
- I’m a good person.
I'm a great guy.

1188
00:43:57,703 --> 00:43:59,137
I got a lot to offer.
This'll be fun.

1189
00:43:59,203 --> 00:44:00,372
I’m a good person.
I'm a great guy.

1190
00:44:00,438 --> 00:44:01,773
I got a lot to offer.
This'll be fun.

1191
00:44:01,840 --> 00:44:03,342
I'm a good person.
I'm a great guy!

1192
00:44:03,408 --> 00:44:04,577
- Okay, okay, Tom.

1193
00:44:04,643 --> 00:44:06,512
Okay, Tom, you're sounding
real confident.

1194
00:44:06,578 --> 00:44:08,247
I think it's time for you
to call up Gypsy

1195
00:44:08,313 --> 00:44:09,448
and ask her on that date.

1196
00:44:09,515 --> 00:44:10,715
Here, I’ll press speed dial
for you.

1197
00:44:10,782 --> 00:44:12,752
- Thank you, thank you.
- Hey, Joel, Tom.

1198
00:44:12,818 --> 00:44:14,853
[ phone dialing ]

1199
00:44:14,920 --> 00:44:17,488
- Tom's just about to ask Gypsy
out on a date,

1200
00:44:17,555 --> 00:44:19,958
and I told him you and I would
set up a scavenger sale

1201
00:44:20,025 --> 00:44:21,493
like we saw
in the dating short.

1202
00:44:21,560 --> 00:44:22,928
- Isn’t that
a little weird, Joel?

1203
00:44:22,995 --> 00:44:24,697
- Yeah, it is. Here, I'll
put it on the speakerphone.

1204
00:44:24,763 --> 00:44:26,332
- I’m a guy.
I'm a great person.

1205
00:44:26,398 --> 00:44:27,365
[ line ringing ]

1206
00:44:27,432 --> 00:44:28,767
- What are you going
to say, huh?

1207
00:44:28,833 --> 00:44:29,868
What are you going to say?
What are you going to ask her?

1208
00:44:29,935 --> 00:44:31,337
What if she doesn’t like you?

1209
00:44:31,403 --> 00:44:33,905
What are you going to do?
I don't think she likes you.

1210
00:44:33,972 --> 00:44:36,442
- Hello?

1211
00:44:36,508 --> 00:44:37,508
Hello?

1212
00:44:37,575 --> 00:44:39,645
- Hello, uh...

1213
00:44:39,712 --> 00:44:41,980
Hello, uh, Gypsy?

1214
00:44:42,047 --> 00:44:44,450
- Yes, what is it?

1215
00:44:44,517 --> 00:44:46,452
I’m really kind of eating.

1216
00:44:46,518 --> 00:44:50,622
- Um, th-this is Tom.

1217
00:44:50,688 --> 00:44:51,623
- Who?

1218
00:44:51,690 --> 00:44:53,125
- Uh, Tom Servo.

1219
00:44:53,192 --> 00:44:55,093
I stand next to you
on the Satellite of Love?

1220
00:44:55,160 --> 00:44:58,330
- Oh. Oh, the red one.

1221
00:44:58,397 --> 00:44:59,898
- See? She remembers you.

1222
00:44:59,965 --> 00:45:01,100
- What do you want?

1223
00:45:01,167 --> 00:45:02,533
- Go for it, baby.

1224
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:05,337
- Well, there’s
this scavenger sale.

1225
00:45:05,403 --> 00:45:06,805
- What’s that?

1226
00:45:06,872 --> 00:45:10,375
- Well, it's just
a scavenger scale--sale,

1227
00:45:10,442 --> 00:45:13,445
and I was wondering if maybe you
might want to go with me

1228
00:45:13,512 --> 00:45:15,713
to this scavenger scale?
Sale.

1229
00:45:15,780 --> 00:45:17,482
- Why would I want to do that?

1230
00:45:17,548 --> 00:45:18,817
- Um, so, anyway,
you want to go?

1231
00:45:18,883 --> 00:45:19,818
- No.
- Great!

1232
00:45:19,885 --> 00:45:20,818
- I said no.
- Please?

1233
00:45:20,885 --> 00:45:21,820
- No.
- Please?

1234
00:45:21,887 --> 00:45:23,188
- No.
- Please?

1235
00:45:23,255 --> 00:45:24,857
I'll say please 10,000 times.
Please, please, please.

1236
00:45:24,923 --> 00:45:26,325
- Oh, okay.

1237
00:45:26,392 --> 00:45:28,627
But we leave when I say.

1238
00:45:28,693 --> 00:45:30,395
- Oh, great!
Okay, see you then.

1239
00:45:30,462 --> 00:45:32,030
Bye-bye, honey.
[ laughing ]

1240
00:45:32,097 --> 00:45:33,032
- All right.

1241
00:45:33,098 --> 00:45:34,398
- Well, fellas,
you can tell right away

1242
00:45:34,467 --> 00:45:36,768
when something like that’s
going to go real smooth.

1243
00:45:36,835 --> 00:45:38,770
In fact, you know what?

1244
00:45:38,837 --> 00:45:40,038
- You’re a good person.

1245
00:45:40,105 --> 00:45:41,072
- I’m a good person.

1246
00:45:41,140 --> 00:45:42,340
- You’ve got a lot to offer.

1247
00:45:42,407 --> 00:45:43,508
- I’ve got a lot to offer.

1248
00:45:43,575 --> 00:45:44,710
- You’re red!
- I'm red!

1249
00:45:44,777 --> 00:45:46,312
- He’s red!
- [ alarms sounding ]

1250
00:45:46,378 --> 00:45:48,513
[ all shouting ]

1251
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:56,922
- And your arms don't work.

1252
00:45:56,988 --> 00:45:58,157
- And my arms don't--
Hey!

1253
00:45:58,223 --> 00:45:59,858
- Sure wish she'd shut up.

1254
00:45:59,892 --> 00:46:01,393
- [ woman crying ]
- Oh, she’s not hurting you.

1255
00:46:01,460 --> 00:46:02,727
Hand me the salt.

1256
00:46:02,795 --> 00:46:04,597
- I set up
the volleyball net.

1257
00:46:04,663 --> 00:46:06,898
- ...if I say she is,
and she gives me a pain.

1258
00:46:06,965 --> 00:46:08,967
- Where’d they get the ladles
and the spices?

1259
00:46:09,033 --> 00:46:10,835
- Alligator’s back there.
- Big one?

1260
00:46:10,902 --> 00:46:12,137
- No, they're tiny.

1261
00:46:12,203 --> 00:46:13,138
- Well, I wouldn't
like to stick my foot

1262
00:46:13,205 --> 00:46:14,438
on top of one in the dark.

1263
00:46:14,507 --> 00:46:16,475
- This about ready?
- In a few minutes.

1264
00:46:16,542 --> 00:46:18,410
- Well, just stand here
and jut some more.

1265
00:46:18,477 --> 00:46:19,678
- Josie, how much longer
you figure

1266
00:46:19,745 --> 00:46:21,078
it’ll take us to get there?

1267
00:46:21,147 --> 00:46:22,713
- Oh, a couple of days,
day and a half if we’re lucky

1268
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:24,315
- Leech look appetizing.

1269
00:46:24,382 --> 00:46:25,517
- Man,
I hope I live long enough

1270
00:46:25,583 --> 00:46:27,085
to get my hands
on them diamonds.

1271
00:46:27,152 --> 00:46:29,120
- Well, they sure are
holding us up plenty.

1272
00:46:29,187 --> 00:46:30,555
- They may be worth it.

1273
00:46:30,622 --> 00:46:32,523
- For what?
- We'll see.

1274
00:46:32,557 --> 00:46:34,192
- Aw, "We’ll see, we’ll see."

1275
00:46:34,258 --> 00:46:36,262
- Look, if I bother you,
go somewhere else.

1276
00:46:36,328 --> 00:46:38,530
- ♪ Da da duh da da ♪

1277
00:46:40,132 --> 00:46:42,968
- Oh, cut it!
Cut it, I said!

1278
00:46:43,035 --> 00:46:44,537
- By God,
I'll kill that dame!

1279
00:46:44,603 --> 00:46:45,703
- You’re killing nobody!

1280
00:46:45,770 --> 00:46:47,005
Now stop it!

1281
00:46:47,072 --> 00:46:49,173
- Some of us aren’t going to get
out of here alive.

1282
00:46:49,240 --> 00:46:50,208
- Oh, really, who?

1283
00:46:50,275 --> 00:46:51,677
Oh, me.

1284
00:46:51,743 --> 00:46:54,012
- Food’s ready, unless
you’d rather fight than eat.

1285
00:46:54,078 --> 00:46:55,480
- Aw, shut up.

1286
00:46:55,547 --> 00:46:57,648
- Well, this is going to be
a great dinner.

1287
00:46:58,817 --> 00:47:00,552
- You know, I feel less
like a hostage

1288
00:47:00,618 --> 00:47:02,053
and more like a friend.

1289
00:47:02,120 --> 00:47:03,322
- Take this over to them.

1290
00:47:03,422 --> 00:47:05,190
- What if we don’t have enough?

1291
00:47:05,257 --> 00:47:06,492
- We got enough.

1292
00:47:06,558 --> 00:47:08,293
- There’s plenty of squirrel
to go around.

1293
00:47:10,528 --> 00:47:13,232
- [ crying ]
- Oh, that dame makes me sick.

1294
00:47:13,298 --> 00:47:15,800
- Okay, who had the Granny’s
Country Omelet with?

1295
00:47:15,867 --> 00:47:17,602
Oh, you need coffee?

1296
00:47:17,668 --> 00:47:19,470
- Please, I want to talk to you.

1297
00:47:19,538 --> 00:47:21,640
- Talk to yourself.

1298
00:47:21,707 --> 00:47:25,543
- Oh, oh! You’re kneeling
on Little Touch.

1299
00:47:25,610 --> 00:47:26,845
- Well, what do I do now?

1300
00:47:26,912 --> 00:47:27,845
Feed him?

1301
00:47:27,913 --> 00:47:29,113
- Why not?

1302
00:47:29,180 --> 00:47:30,315
- Does he need changing?

1303
00:47:30,382 --> 00:47:31,917
- Untie his hands
till he’s through.

1304
00:47:33,418 --> 00:47:35,020
- Mmm.
Really great grub.

1305
00:47:35,087 --> 00:47:37,688
- [ crying ] Really great grub,
yum, yum.

1306
00:47:39,825 --> 00:47:42,160
- Uh, honey,
will you pass the salt?

1307
00:47:43,595 --> 00:47:44,763
- Mm.

1308
00:47:44,830 --> 00:47:46,698
- You know, I've
always heard bad things

1309
00:47:46,765 --> 00:47:48,467
about being held hostage.

1310
00:47:51,737 --> 00:47:54,038
- Jab Conners?
- Grunt Conners?

1311
00:47:54,105 --> 00:47:56,140
- Link.

1312
00:47:56,207 --> 00:47:57,575
- Enjoy yourself.

1313
00:47:57,642 --> 00:47:58,843
- I just did.

1314
00:47:58,910 --> 00:47:59,845
- What’s for dessert?

1315
00:48:01,347 --> 00:48:03,015
- Tuna wiggle.

1316
00:48:05,083 --> 00:48:06,585
- Come on,
what’s for dessert?

1317
00:48:06,652 --> 00:48:08,487
Aren't we even
having dessert?

1318
00:48:10,522 --> 00:48:13,058
- Boy, you just can’t keep away
from him, can you?

1319
00:48:13,125 --> 00:48:15,527
- Better than not being able
to get near him.

1320
00:48:15,593 --> 00:48:17,395
- Who'd like a drink?

1321
00:48:17,462 --> 00:48:18,597
- Man, who wouldn’t?

1322
00:48:18,663 --> 00:48:19,765
- I’ll have a Rob Roy.

1323
00:48:19,832 --> 00:48:21,065
- Take a look
in my blanket over there.

1324
00:48:21,132 --> 00:48:22,533
- You’re kidding!

1325
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:25,303
- Oh, those kids, I’ve never
seen them so happy.

1326
00:48:25,370 --> 00:48:27,705
- It’s not enough
to slow us up tomorrow.

1327
00:48:27,772 --> 00:48:29,040
- It doesn’t get
any skuzzier than this.

1328
00:48:29,107 --> 00:48:31,510
- Four years is
a long time to be in the jug.

1329
00:48:31,577 --> 00:48:32,677
- Oww!

1330
00:48:32,743 --> 00:48:33,945
- She was in the jug?

1331
00:48:34,012 --> 00:48:35,613
- Hey, give me some,
too, you pig.

1332
00:48:35,680 --> 00:48:37,682
- Hey, come on,
bring it over here!

1333
00:48:39,952 --> 00:48:42,920
- [ laughs ] After a prison
break and hostage taking,

1334
00:48:42,988 --> 00:48:45,790
it’s back to the lodge
for a smooth Canadian Club.

1335
00:48:45,857 --> 00:48:47,392
- Oh, no!

1336
00:48:47,458 --> 00:48:48,493
- Oh! Oh!

1337
00:48:48,560 --> 00:48:50,828
- Oh, Josie, this is crazy.

1338
00:48:50,895 --> 00:48:52,297
- So it’s crazy.

1339
00:48:52,363 --> 00:48:55,633
- Nardo girls never run around
in pants like a bunch of boys.

1340
00:48:55,700 --> 00:48:58,137
- What, they get drunk
and they make shorts?

1341
00:48:58,203 --> 00:49:00,338
- Yeah,
they’re Daisy Mae shorts.

1342
00:49:00,405 --> 00:49:01,640
- Mmm.

1343
00:49:01,707 --> 00:49:03,775
- Hey, Vera, I want mine cut off
a little shorter.

1344
00:49:03,842 --> 00:49:05,010
- Do it yourself.

1345
00:49:05,077 --> 00:49:07,878
- The purpose of the movie
finally revealed.

1346
00:49:07,945 --> 00:49:09,313
- [ calling ] Oh, Touch?

1347
00:49:09,380 --> 00:49:12,083
- Maybe he goes for girls
in little blue sweaters.

1348
00:49:12,117 --> 00:49:14,787
- Ah, maybe, sure.
Um, hmm...

1349
00:49:18,357 --> 00:49:19,892
- Please leave me alone!

1350
00:49:19,958 --> 00:49:22,027
- These are stirrup pants!
I beg you!

1351
00:49:22,093 --> 00:49:24,628
- I’ll give you anything.
- Like what?

1352
00:49:24,697 --> 00:49:27,165
- Listen to me.
Just get me out of here, honey,

1353
00:49:27,232 --> 00:49:28,300
and I’ll give you
whatever you want.

1354
00:49:28,367 --> 00:49:30,202
- How much?

1355
00:49:30,268 --> 00:49:31,470
- Whatever you want.

1356
00:49:31,537 --> 00:49:32,637
- I want
your sleeveless blue dress.

1357
00:49:32,703 --> 00:49:34,572
- A thousand? 10.

1358
00:49:34,638 --> 00:49:37,275
- And your boyfriend,
you buying him, too?

1359
00:49:37,342 --> 00:49:39,277
- I don’t care.
Just get me out of here.

1360
00:49:39,343 --> 00:49:42,013
My daddy will give you
whatever you want.

1361
00:49:42,080 --> 00:49:43,548
- Hear that, handsome?

1362
00:49:43,615 --> 00:49:44,850
Your girlfriend's trying
to buy her way out,

1363
00:49:44,917 --> 00:49:46,785
but she doesn’t care
what happens to you.

1364
00:49:46,852 --> 00:49:47,918
- Yes, I did.
Thank you .

1365
00:49:47,985 --> 00:49:49,087
- Isn't that right?

1366
00:49:49,153 --> 00:49:50,088
- A little off the sides.

1367
00:49:50,155 --> 00:49:51,623
- Get me out of here!

1368
00:49:51,690 --> 00:49:53,558
- Oh, I wouldn’t wear your lousy
sweater if you gave it to me!

1369
00:49:53,625 --> 00:49:55,027
- [ crying ]

1370
00:49:56,428 --> 00:49:57,795
- Nice kid.

1371
00:49:57,862 --> 00:49:59,297
Sell her man
right down the river.

1372
00:49:59,363 --> 00:50:01,500
- Yeah, some women
have no class.

1373
00:50:01,567 --> 00:50:02,633
- I sure miss Nicky.

1374
00:50:02,700 --> 00:50:04,737
- Yeah. Who’s Nicky?

1375
00:50:04,803 --> 00:50:06,738
- Joey, Mike.

1376
00:50:06,805 --> 00:50:08,907
- You can just forget
about missing Mike.

1377
00:50:08,973 --> 00:50:10,742
- Would we have a ball
with those diamonds

1378
00:50:10,808 --> 00:50:12,743
if the guys were
still with us?

1379
00:50:12,810 --> 00:50:14,145
- No. Yes.

1380
00:50:14,212 --> 00:50:15,980
- I plan to have a ball
without them.

1381
00:50:16,080 --> 00:50:17,448
I'm going to go
down to Mexico,

1382
00:50:17,515 --> 00:50:19,183
and I’m going to buy myself
a town.

1383
00:50:19,250 --> 00:50:20,418
- Huh?
- Huh?

1384
00:50:20,485 --> 00:50:21,520
- You’re drunk.

1385
00:50:21,587 --> 00:50:22,720
What do you want with a town?

1386
00:50:22,787 --> 00:50:24,222
- Well, you’d always have
a place to park.

1387
00:50:24,288 --> 00:50:25,523
- I may be drunk,

1388
00:50:25,590 --> 00:50:27,092
but I'm going to buy a town,

1389
00:50:27,158 --> 00:50:28,560
I'm going to buy
everybody in it,

1390
00:50:28,627 --> 00:50:30,228
and I’m going to order them
around the rest of my life.

1391
00:50:30,295 --> 00:50:31,797
- Why, don’t you have goals?

1392
00:50:31,863 --> 00:50:32,963
- You got a better idea?

1393
00:50:33,030 --> 00:50:35,300
- I got a better idea.

1394
00:50:35,367 --> 00:50:38,870
- I’m going
to start a sod farm.

1395
00:50:38,937 --> 00:50:41,272
- Going to find me a doctor

1396
00:50:41,338 --> 00:50:43,642
and have him change
my whole face around.

1397
00:50:43,708 --> 00:50:44,708
- To the back.

1398
00:50:44,777 --> 00:50:45,810
- Cut it up.

1399
00:50:45,877 --> 00:50:47,812
- You ain’t that ugly.

1400
00:50:47,845 --> 00:50:51,248
- I ain’t ugly at all,
and you know it.

1401
00:50:51,315 --> 00:50:53,752
But I ain’t going to look
like me no more.

1402
00:50:53,818 --> 00:50:55,687
- I'm going to look
like Tito Puente.

1403
00:50:55,753 --> 00:50:59,090
- I'm going to keep
the old little address book,

1404
00:50:59,157 --> 00:51:02,160
and I'm going to start
with the judge first

1405
00:51:02,227 --> 00:51:04,095
who sent the guys
to the chair.

1406
00:51:04,162 --> 00:51:05,730
- Did they all go
to the same chair?

1407
00:51:05,797 --> 00:51:09,567
- Then all the folks
of the jury,

1408
00:51:09,633 --> 00:51:11,937
and I'm going
to louse them all up.

1409
00:51:12,003 --> 00:51:13,505
- How do you mean?

1410
00:51:13,572 --> 00:51:15,973
- Going to break up
all their happy homes.

1411
00:51:16,040 --> 00:51:18,443
- Boy, she really slides
into her sentences, doesn’t she?

1412
00:51:18,510 --> 00:51:21,880
- Going to make
their wives hate them,

1413
00:51:21,947 --> 00:51:23,615
and their kids.

1414
00:51:23,682 --> 00:51:25,683
- Well, I’ll do something
to their kids.

1415
00:51:25,750 --> 00:51:28,187
- I’m going
to louse them all up!

1416
00:51:28,253 --> 00:51:30,655
[ laughing ]

1417
00:51:30,722 --> 00:51:33,392
- I’m still
with the town idea.

1418
00:51:33,458 --> 00:51:34,592
- Good for you.

1419
00:51:34,658 --> 00:51:36,260
- What are you going
to do, Josie?

1420
00:51:36,327 --> 00:51:37,528
- Mm, same thing.

1421
00:51:37,595 --> 00:51:38,997
- I tell you, I got a plan.

1422
00:51:39,063 --> 00:51:41,365
I'm going to get me a big house
south of the border,

1423
00:51:41,432 --> 00:51:43,668
and I’m going to rent rooms
to everybody that’s on the lam.

1424
00:51:43,735 --> 00:51:46,403
- The old lady in the shoe.

1425
00:51:46,472 --> 00:51:47,438
- Sure, why not?

1426
00:51:47,505 --> 00:51:49,440
I figure I can make
a good living

1427
00:51:49,507 --> 00:51:52,310
and make plenty of trouble
for the cops at the same time.

1428
00:51:52,377 --> 00:51:55,080
- I’m going to star
in The Mothers-in-Law.

1429
00:51:55,147 --> 00:51:57,715
- I hope to make detective--
Ooh!

1430
00:51:57,782 --> 00:51:59,450
- I just want to be by myself,
that’s all.

1431
00:51:59,517 --> 00:52:02,153
- A lone wolf.

1432
00:52:02,220 --> 00:52:03,488
- Awoo!

1433
00:52:03,555 --> 00:52:04,655
- You can’t trust them.

1434
00:52:04,722 --> 00:52:08,693
- Now, come on,
we were having a good time!

1435
00:52:08,760 --> 00:52:11,095
- Touch, how about you?

1436
00:52:12,430 --> 00:52:14,532
- Girls, let’s do this
again sometime.

1437
00:52:15,667 --> 00:52:16,868
- Mmm, 10W-40.

1438
00:52:16,935 --> 00:52:18,002
Well, it's good, though.

1439
00:52:18,068 --> 00:52:20,405
- I’ll take the first watch.

1440
00:52:20,472 --> 00:52:22,340
Guess he’s
not going anyplace.

1441
00:52:22,407 --> 00:52:24,642
Thanks for the drink.

1442
00:52:24,708 --> 00:52:26,945
- Sure can hold plenty
of it.

1443
00:52:27,012 --> 00:52:28,680
- You don’t do
so bad yourself.

1444
00:52:28,747 --> 00:52:32,050
- Want to take that across
the street and get deposit?

1445
00:52:32,117 --> 00:52:34,118
- I love you, Sir Booze.

1446
00:52:34,185 --> 00:52:35,120
Bye-bye.

1447
00:52:37,788 --> 00:52:40,292
[ all making vomiting noises ]

1448
00:52:42,960 --> 00:52:45,563
- Oh, God,
what did we do last night?

1449
00:52:45,630 --> 00:52:46,865
What was in that stuff?

1450
00:52:46,932 --> 00:52:48,667
[ vomiting noises ]

1451
00:52:48,733 --> 00:52:50,902
- Oh, no, they forgot
to hang the hostages

1452
00:52:50,968 --> 00:52:52,737
10 feet off the ground.

1453
00:52:52,803 --> 00:52:55,240
- [ snoring] Hiccup!

1454
00:52:55,340 --> 00:52:56,608
[ snoring ]

1455
00:52:56,675 --> 00:52:59,177
- Okay, who’s for lizard
biscuits with cypress gravy?

1456
00:53:00,345 --> 00:53:02,780
- Hmm?

1457
00:53:02,847 --> 00:53:04,648
- Hey!

1458
00:53:04,715 --> 00:53:06,483
- What?

1459
00:53:06,552 --> 00:53:08,787
Oh, I’ve been shot, okay.

1460
00:53:08,853 --> 00:53:10,788
- She’s at the Y.

1461
00:53:10,855 --> 00:53:13,658
- Help! Help!

1462
00:53:13,725 --> 00:53:15,260
- What on...?

1463
00:53:15,327 --> 00:53:16,995
- I don’t think she can swim.

1464
00:53:17,062 --> 00:53:18,397
- Wait a minute,
I'll swim out here

1465
00:53:18,463 --> 00:53:19,898
and ask her if she can swim.

1466
00:53:24,068 --> 00:53:26,672
- [ imitating
sound of speedboat ]

1467
00:53:26,705 --> 00:53:28,138
- Help!

1468
00:53:28,205 --> 00:53:30,375
- Just stand up!
You're in the shallow end!

1469
00:53:33,110 --> 00:53:36,213
- [ imitating engine revving ]

1470
00:53:36,280 --> 00:53:37,915
- By the boat.
- I see him.

1471
00:53:37,982 --> 00:53:39,050
It’s going to get her!

1472
00:53:39,117 --> 00:53:40,818
- Quick, Josie,
cut me loose!

1473
00:53:40,885 --> 00:53:43,755
- [ gasping ]

1474
00:53:45,423 --> 00:53:49,227
- [ humming along
with dramatic music ]

1475
00:53:49,293 --> 00:53:51,630
- Wait, how’s he going to get
to the pool where she is?

1476
00:53:51,697 --> 00:53:54,165
- Help! Help!

1477
00:53:54,232 --> 00:53:56,333
- I’m a-comin',
I’m a-comin'.

1478
00:53:57,802 --> 00:53:59,737
- Oh, help!

1479
00:53:59,837 --> 00:54:02,307
- Wait, that’s a mud puppy!

1480
00:54:02,373 --> 00:54:06,645
- If only David Hasselhoff
were here!

1481
00:54:06,712 --> 00:54:08,813
- [ humming along
with dramatic music ]

1482
00:54:08,880 --> 00:54:11,515
- Oh, that’s a problem.
I'll go report in.

1483
00:54:14,518 --> 00:54:16,988
- Boy, I can’t wait until
all these movies come together.

1484
00:54:17,055 --> 00:54:18,457
- Mmm, think of it.

1485
00:54:23,728 --> 00:54:25,997
- You know, it's hard to keep
your head above water

1486
00:54:26,063 --> 00:54:27,765
when you’re up to your ass
in alligators.

1487
00:54:27,832 --> 00:54:29,733
- I got a poster like that.

1488
00:54:29,800 --> 00:54:32,337
- I’ve got him!

1489
00:54:32,403 --> 00:54:33,338
No, no, help!

1490
00:54:33,405 --> 00:54:34,638
Blub blub blub!

1491
00:54:34,705 --> 00:54:36,842
- So you want to make shoes
out of me, huh?

1492
00:54:36,908 --> 00:54:38,843
I got your shoes right here.

1493
00:54:45,750 --> 00:54:47,652
- Well, wait a minute.
Didn't we forget--

1494
00:54:47,718 --> 00:54:49,387
Oh, my girlfriend!

1495
00:54:49,453 --> 00:54:50,855
- She was
in a pool across town.

1496
00:54:50,922 --> 00:54:52,357
They couldn’t
have saved her anyway.

1497
00:54:54,625 --> 00:54:57,328
- So, uh, what
are you doing next Saturday?

1498
00:54:57,395 --> 00:54:58,763
Give you a lift?

1499
00:55:00,032 --> 00:55:02,700
- Hey, it’s
a wet Pendleton contest.

1500
00:55:03,868 --> 00:55:05,370
- She’s a man!

1501
00:55:05,437 --> 00:55:07,138
- Uh-oh.
- Huh?

1502
00:55:07,205 --> 00:55:08,138
- I'm sorry.

1503
00:55:08,205 --> 00:55:09,640
- Apology accepted.

1504
00:55:09,707 --> 00:55:11,442
- Yeah.

1505
00:55:11,508 --> 00:55:13,345
- Oh, man,
wish you hadn’t done that.

1506
00:55:15,113 --> 00:55:18,082
- Sorry for what?

1507
00:55:18,148 --> 00:55:19,983
- Sorry for not saving
her life.

1508
00:55:20,052 --> 00:55:22,320
- Oh, her.
It was a first date.

1509
00:55:22,387 --> 00:55:24,255
- Making you risk your life.

1510
00:55:26,590 --> 00:55:28,258
- Was that supposed
to be a moment?

1511
00:55:28,325 --> 00:55:29,460
- Yeah.

1512
00:55:30,628 --> 00:55:33,197
- Hey, the boat handles
real well now!

1513
00:55:33,263 --> 00:55:35,167
Making good time, too!

1514
00:55:39,037 --> 00:55:40,838
- Yes, every available man.

1515
00:55:40,905 --> 00:55:42,640
I want
that entire area surrounded.

1516
00:55:42,707 --> 00:55:44,108
- Oui, mon capitaine.

1517
00:55:44,175 --> 00:55:46,177
- Any man that gets too close,
I’ll personally break him.

1518
00:55:46,243 --> 00:55:47,445
- Way to be.

1519
00:55:47,512 --> 00:55:49,780
- Try anything,
Lieutenant Hampton's through.

1520
00:55:49,847 --> 00:55:52,083
- Hey, they traded up.

1521
00:55:52,150 --> 00:55:53,985
- Oh, they got hats
and everything.

1522
00:55:59,623 --> 00:56:00,758
- Chief?
- Yeah.

1523
00:56:00,825 --> 00:56:01,993
- Wait, didn’t
I just talk to you?

1524
00:56:02,060 --> 00:56:04,228
- No, only one helicopter.

1525
00:56:04,295 --> 00:56:06,898
Personally tell the pilot
not to get too close.

1526
00:56:06,965 --> 00:56:08,132
He mustn’t hover
over the scene.

1527
00:56:08,198 --> 00:56:10,968
- Now, wait, wait,
I have no idea.

1528
00:56:11,035 --> 00:56:12,570
Wait a minute.
I didn't order this.

1529
00:56:12,637 --> 00:56:14,005
I meant to put you on hold.

1530
00:56:14,072 --> 00:56:16,173
- What’s the matter with
that unit on the left?

1531
00:56:16,240 --> 00:56:18,175
All right, pull them back!

1532
00:56:18,242 --> 00:56:20,245
We must not risk being seen!

1533
00:56:20,312 --> 00:56:21,245
- Allez!

1534
00:56:23,380 --> 00:56:24,648
- Milk! Milk!

1535
00:56:24,715 --> 00:56:26,985
Get your 2%, get your butter,
sticks or patties!

1536
00:56:27,052 --> 00:56:29,387
Milk!

1537
00:56:29,453 --> 00:56:32,723
- Josie, how many more thousand
miles we got to go?

1538
00:56:32,790 --> 00:56:34,225
- About five more miles.

1539
00:56:34,292 --> 00:56:36,360
It's rough. I don’t want
to try it at night.

1540
00:56:36,427 --> 00:56:38,095
We’ll stop
at the first good place.

1541
00:56:38,128 --> 00:56:39,763
- Are you sure
you can find them?

1542
00:56:39,830 --> 00:56:42,100
- You could blindfold me,
and I could find them.

1543
00:56:42,167 --> 00:56:43,435
- There’s an extra leg
in there.

1544
00:56:43,502 --> 00:56:45,703
- Still gonna find some help
spending the loot.

1545
00:56:45,770 --> 00:56:47,538
- If Nicky was here,
he'd be ordering you around

1546
00:56:47,605 --> 00:56:49,107
just like he always did.

1547
00:56:49,173 --> 00:56:51,943
- You know what? I miss being
told what to do.

1548
00:56:52,010 --> 00:56:53,745
Oh, that looks
like a good place.

1549
00:56:53,812 --> 00:56:55,680
We’ll pull in there.

1550
00:56:58,115 --> 00:57:00,017
- Okay, now,
remember our rule--

1551
00:57:00,083 --> 00:57:02,153
only one dead at each place.

1552
00:57:04,122 --> 00:57:05,423
- Hey,
if they got drunk again,

1553
00:57:05,490 --> 00:57:07,225
they won’t have any pants
left at all.

1554
00:57:07,292 --> 00:57:09,227
- Drink, drink, drink, drink!

1555
00:57:09,293 --> 00:57:11,062
- So far, so good.
Nobody dead yet.

1556
00:57:11,162 --> 00:57:13,430
- Still beats the prison.

1557
00:57:15,367 --> 00:57:17,035
- Josie, if the cops
are waiting for us,

1558
00:57:17,102 --> 00:57:19,170
how do you figure we’re going
to get the diamonds out of here?

1559
00:57:19,237 --> 00:57:20,505
- Take a powder.

1560
00:57:20,572 --> 00:57:21,705
- Sure I can’t help you?

1561
00:57:21,772 --> 00:57:23,742
- I think we can manage
without you. Get lost.

1562
00:57:23,808 --> 00:57:25,177
- Well, I’ll see you
at lunch then.

1563
00:57:25,243 --> 00:57:26,177
I’m outta here.

1564
00:57:26,243 --> 00:57:27,578
- Too bad. Nice guy.

1565
00:57:27,645 --> 00:57:29,113
- Huh! He’s nothing.

1566
00:57:29,180 --> 00:57:31,782
- Hey, any chance
for a drink of water?

1567
00:57:31,850 --> 00:57:33,518
- I’ll get him some.

1568
00:57:33,585 --> 00:57:35,520
- Oh, excuse me, miss.

1569
00:57:39,657 --> 00:57:42,460
Come to
the Church in the Wildwood.

1570
00:57:45,763 --> 00:57:47,032
- I thirst.

1571
00:57:47,098 --> 00:57:48,098
- Have a drink.

1572
00:57:48,165 --> 00:57:49,467
- Don’t mind if I do.

1573
00:57:49,533 --> 00:57:51,335
- Oh, good, 'cause
that’s what’s happening.

1574
00:57:51,402 --> 00:57:52,570
- I don’t get it.

1575
00:57:52,637 --> 00:57:53,838
- It’s just water.

1576
00:57:53,905 --> 00:57:55,005
- You will.

1577
00:57:57,475 --> 00:57:59,010
- Just what is it with you?

1578
00:57:59,077 --> 00:58:00,178
- Stuff.

1579
00:58:01,778 --> 00:58:03,247
- Thanks.

1580
00:58:03,313 --> 00:58:04,315
- Water?

1581
00:58:05,850 --> 00:58:08,385
- We got to get the wood
before it gets dark.

1582
00:58:08,452 --> 00:58:09,853
- I’ll get some.

1583
00:58:12,990 --> 00:58:14,025
- Oh, hi.

1584
00:58:16,862 --> 00:58:19,830
- Not you again.
We can't keep doing this.

1585
00:58:19,897 --> 00:58:22,033
- Why don’t you tell me
the story of your life?

1586
00:58:22,100 --> 00:58:24,202
- Before I went into crime?

1587
00:58:24,268 --> 00:58:25,837
- You were never in it.

1588
00:58:25,903 --> 00:58:28,272
- Well, don’t tell my friends.

1589
00:58:28,338 --> 00:58:29,573
Are you all right?

1590
00:58:29,640 --> 00:58:31,877
- Oh, sure, just great.

1591
00:58:31,943 --> 00:58:33,443
- Wrists sore?

1592
00:58:33,510 --> 00:58:35,680
- Not too sore.

1593
00:58:35,747 --> 00:58:36,948
- So how
have your stools been?

1594
00:58:37,015 --> 00:58:38,883
Mmph mmph!

1595
00:58:40,585 --> 00:58:42,087
- Try that again,
and I’ll kill you!

1596
00:58:43,153 --> 00:58:45,022
- Now what’s going on?

1597
00:58:45,088 --> 00:58:46,892
- Oh, I was just checking
his rope for the night,

1598
00:58:46,958 --> 00:58:48,092
and he tried to get fresh.

1599
00:58:48,158 --> 00:58:50,295
- You sure it wasn’t your idea?

1600
00:58:50,362 --> 00:58:52,130
- I’m sure.

1601
00:58:52,197 --> 00:58:56,033
- Next time,
we kidnap Ernest Borgnine.

1602
00:58:56,100 --> 00:58:57,568
- How’s that?

1603
00:58:57,635 --> 00:58:58,870
- You didn’t have to cut
off his hands.

1604
00:58:58,937 --> 00:59:00,938
- Hi, what’s up?

1605
00:59:01,005 --> 00:59:03,642
- Cut it out, you two.

1606
00:59:03,708 --> 00:59:06,143
- I think there’s too many cooks
in the kitchen.

1607
00:59:06,210 --> 00:59:08,647
- I always notice you’re around
to protect him.

1608
00:59:08,713 --> 00:59:09,813
- So what?

1609
00:59:09,880 --> 00:59:11,015
- So I don’t like it,
that’s all.

1610
00:59:11,082 --> 00:59:12,283
I think there’s something
between them.

1611
00:59:12,350 --> 00:59:14,152
- Yeah, see?
Something between them.

1612
00:59:14,218 --> 00:59:16,453
- That's no rule.

1613
00:59:16,520 --> 00:59:18,122
- Girls, plenty of Touch
to go around.

1614
00:59:18,188 --> 00:59:19,557
- That gripes me.

1615
00:59:19,623 --> 00:59:22,027
- Well, knock it off
and let’s get some shuteye.

1616
00:59:22,093 --> 00:59:25,263
- Yeah, sure, warden.

1617
00:59:25,330 --> 00:59:27,532
You kind of go for that dame,
don’t you?

1618
00:59:27,598 --> 00:59:28,933
- Bother you, Red?

1619
00:59:30,200 --> 00:59:31,668
- It’s orange, not red!

1620
00:59:33,370 --> 00:59:35,105
- I wouldn’t.

1621
00:59:35,172 --> 00:59:36,773
- What? What?

1622
00:59:38,542 --> 00:59:40,345
- Can’t get enough
of that shot.

1623
00:59:40,412 --> 00:59:41,878
- Hey, who TP’d the swamp?

1624
00:59:41,947 --> 00:59:43,782
[ piano music ]

1625
00:59:43,848 --> 00:59:46,417
- ♪ As time goes on... ♪

1626
00:59:46,483 --> 00:59:48,318
- Keep any eye out
for gators, will you?

1627
00:59:48,385 --> 00:59:50,688
I’d like to get out of here
with the same pieces I got in.

1628
00:59:50,755 --> 00:59:52,457
- Well, that could be improved.

1629
00:59:52,523 --> 00:59:54,158
- Yeah, says who?

1630
00:59:54,225 --> 00:59:55,627
- Hey, isn't Vera coming in?

1631
00:59:55,693 --> 00:59:57,228
- Nah. She’s still asleep.

1632
00:59:57,295 --> 00:59:59,163
She must think we’re working.

1633
00:59:59,230 --> 01:00:00,665
- Whoa, hold on.

1634
01:00:00,732 --> 01:00:01,665
[ chuckling ]

1635
01:00:07,705 --> 01:00:10,007
- After we left clam flowage
that day,

1636
01:00:10,073 --> 01:00:12,110
we knew that one day soon
we would return

1637
01:00:12,177 --> 01:00:14,212
to seek
the wily bucketmouth.

1638
01:00:14,278 --> 01:00:17,748
Next up, Myrna
with a new carp-ball recipe.

1639
01:00:21,852 --> 01:00:24,322
- Do not bring
your padding here.

1640
01:00:27,325 --> 01:00:30,728
- Looks like the bayou’s
all clogged up.

1641
01:00:30,795 --> 01:00:32,197
- Hmm? Hmm.

1642
01:00:32,263 --> 01:00:33,197
- Hey!

1643
01:00:33,263 --> 01:00:35,600
- Hey!
- Rog?

1644
01:00:35,667 --> 01:00:39,103
- Hey, Roger’s getting footage
for another movie.

1645
01:00:39,170 --> 01:00:41,438
- Uh, Rog, over here, buddy.

1646
01:00:41,505 --> 01:00:43,207
Rog? Uh, Rog?

1647
01:00:43,273 --> 01:00:44,708
Roger!

1648
01:00:44,775 --> 01:00:47,212
Roger, would you please
cut with the thing?

1649
01:00:47,278 --> 01:00:48,880
- Man, what do we do now?

1650
01:00:48,947 --> 01:00:50,782
- It sure wasn’t this way
the last time.

1651
01:00:50,848 --> 01:00:52,150
- No, but it sure is now.

1652
01:00:52,217 --> 01:00:53,417
- They got a flat?

1653
01:00:53,483 --> 01:00:54,752
- Do we have to go
through this stuff?

1654
01:00:54,818 --> 01:00:56,487
- Right down the middle.
- Why can't we go around?

1655
01:00:56,553 --> 01:00:58,655
- And take a chance
on getting lost?

1656
01:00:58,723 --> 01:01:00,057
We could be wandering
around this mess

1657
01:01:00,123 --> 01:01:02,327
for the rest of our lives,
which wouldn’t be long.

1658
01:01:02,393 --> 01:01:04,495
- Looks like this stuff
will catch on the propeller.

1659
01:01:04,562 --> 01:01:05,963
Do we have
to row through this?

1660
01:01:06,030 --> 01:01:07,965
- Stop fighting!
Just stop fighting!

1661
01:01:08,032 --> 01:01:10,635
- All right, how we going
to get through this mess?

1662
01:01:10,702 --> 01:01:12,970
- We’ll pull
ourselves through.

1663
01:01:13,037 --> 01:01:14,838
It’s only
a couple of feet deep.

1664
01:01:14,905 --> 01:01:15,907
We’ll take turns.

1665
01:01:15,973 --> 01:01:18,777
- At Touch.

1666
01:01:18,843 --> 01:01:21,378
- Uh, will you
send this paddle?

1667
01:01:21,445 --> 01:01:23,113
Oooh-oh!

1668
01:01:23,180 --> 01:01:25,048
- How long’s it going to take us
to get through, Josie?

1669
01:01:25,115 --> 01:01:26,550
- Aw, how do I know?

1670
01:01:26,650 --> 01:01:28,352
All I know
is there’s no other way.

1671
01:01:32,357 --> 01:01:35,025
- Giddy up. Ha ha.
Just kidding, girls.

1672
01:01:41,032 --> 01:01:42,967
- Hey, don’t go to sleep
on the job!

1673
01:01:43,033 --> 01:01:44,302
- Vera, shut up.

1674
01:01:44,368 --> 01:01:46,170
- [ crying ] Why can’t we
just joke anymore?

1675
01:01:46,237 --> 01:01:48,072
- Oh, you two take a turn.

1676
01:01:48,138 --> 01:01:51,108
- Maybe they should
all just walk.

1677
01:01:51,175 --> 01:01:52,943
- Nice work, huh?
- Yeah.

1678
01:01:53,010 --> 01:01:54,645
- Wait a minute,
this is an actual trick.

1679
01:01:54,712 --> 01:01:56,313
This hasn’t even been edited.

1680
01:01:56,380 --> 01:01:58,315
- This calls for
not taking any chances.

1681
01:01:58,382 --> 01:02:00,752
We keep his hands tied.

1682
01:02:00,818 --> 01:02:02,018
- Chinese fire drill!

1683
01:02:02,087 --> 01:02:03,187
- Don't make
a lot of sense to me

1684
01:02:03,253 --> 01:02:04,555
why we should do all the work.

1685
01:02:04,622 --> 01:02:07,992
- Oh, this stinking
swamp water stinks!

1686
01:02:08,058 --> 01:02:09,227
- Oh, that’s Touch.

1687
01:02:09,293 --> 01:02:12,897
- Why don’t you two stop griping
and get to work?

1688
01:02:12,963 --> 01:02:14,432
- Give me that paddle!
I want the thing part of it!

1689
01:02:14,498 --> 01:02:15,767
- Give me that!
I want the wide end!

1690
01:02:15,833 --> 01:02:17,368
- I want the thin part
of the paddle!

1691
01:02:17,435 --> 01:02:20,037
- I'm gonna smack you!

1692
01:02:21,972 --> 01:02:23,473
- ♪ Old man river ♪

1693
01:02:23,540 --> 01:02:25,577
- Look,
it’s clear water up ahead.

1694
01:02:25,643 --> 01:02:27,378
- Huh? Credence Clearwater
up ahead?

1695
01:02:27,445 --> 01:02:29,180
- No, no.
- And Canned Heat?

1696
01:02:29,247 --> 01:02:30,882
- ♪ Goin' up country ♪

1697
01:02:30,948 --> 01:02:32,817
♪ Don't you wanna go? ♪

1698
01:02:32,883 --> 01:02:34,552
- Well, that scene
was really important.

1699
01:02:34,618 --> 01:02:37,155
- As crises go,
that wasn’t that bad.

1700
01:02:38,823 --> 01:02:41,092
- As we left
the clam flowage that day,

1701
01:02:41,158 --> 01:02:43,027
we knew that one day soon
we would return

1702
01:02:43,093 --> 01:02:44,828
to seek
the wily bucketmouth.

1703
01:02:44,895 --> 01:02:46,330
Did I just say that?

1704
01:02:46,397 --> 01:02:48,132
- Yeah.

1705
01:02:48,198 --> 01:02:51,068
- They're swamp diamonds
'cause on account of the fact

1706
01:02:51,135 --> 01:02:54,005
they’re looking for diamonds
that are hidden in the...

1707
01:02:54,072 --> 01:02:55,907
- Swamp.
- Swamp.

1708
01:02:55,973 --> 01:02:57,508
- Wouldn't it be funny
if it just turned out

1709
01:02:57,575 --> 01:02:58,943
to be swamp cubic zirconia?

1710
01:02:59,010 --> 01:03:00,043
- Mm, no.

1711
01:03:00,110 --> 01:03:02,713
- This is really
The Neverending Story.

1712
01:03:02,780 --> 01:03:05,315
- How’s by you?
- Fine!

1713
01:03:05,382 --> 01:03:07,017
[ somber brass playing ]

1714
01:03:07,083 --> 01:03:10,087
- Herb Alpert plays the haunting
Swamp Diamond love theme.

1715
01:03:11,688 --> 01:03:13,357
- [ sighs ]

1716
01:03:13,423 --> 01:03:15,660
I could use an overdose
of Dramamine right now.

1717
01:03:15,727 --> 01:03:16,660
- Mm-hmm.

1718
01:03:19,497 --> 01:03:22,833
- Journey
to the beginning of time!

1719
01:03:26,737 --> 01:03:29,073
- You know, sometimes it's
just nice to look at the scenery

1720
01:03:29,140 --> 01:03:30,307
and just not talk.

1721
01:03:30,373 --> 01:03:31,708
- Mmm.
- Mmm.

1722
01:03:31,775 --> 01:03:33,110
- Right here.

1723
01:03:36,547 --> 01:03:38,582
- Man, I thought we were
never going to make it!

1724
01:03:38,648 --> 01:03:40,685
- Gee, I sure can’t wait to get
my hands on those diamonds!

1725
01:03:40,752 --> 01:03:42,420
- They must be
at a Stuckey's.

1726
01:03:45,523 --> 01:03:47,692
- Barely more sophisticated
than To Catch a Thief,

1727
01:03:47,758 --> 01:03:49,360
but still pretty good.

1728
01:03:49,427 --> 01:03:51,095
- I guess we steered
to the right spot.

1729
01:03:51,162 --> 01:03:52,397
- What are they,

1730
01:03:52,463 --> 01:03:54,098
digging for a six-pack
of Lone Star or something?

1731
01:03:54,165 --> 01:03:55,398
- It’s in the boat.

1732
01:03:55,465 --> 01:03:56,600
- Hey, bring me a shovel!

1733
01:03:56,667 --> 01:03:59,470
- Shovel coming up!

1734
01:03:59,537 --> 01:04:01,605
- Hey, how long you been here?

1735
01:04:01,672 --> 01:04:03,340
- Ropes cutting your wrists?

1736
01:04:03,407 --> 01:04:04,508
- What wrists?

1737
01:04:04,575 --> 01:04:05,508
- What bris?

1738
01:04:05,543 --> 01:04:06,777
- I wish I could untie you.

1739
01:04:06,843 --> 01:04:08,412
- I wish you could, too.

1740
01:04:08,478 --> 01:04:10,548
- Hurry up!

1741
01:04:10,615 --> 01:04:13,117
- If I wasn’t tied,
we could jump them now.

1742
01:04:13,183 --> 01:04:14,785
- Or you could all jump me.

1743
01:04:14,852 --> 01:04:16,453
