1986
01:13:59,002 --> 01:14:00,570
- I don’t know
how she did it.

1987
01:14:00,637 --> 01:14:03,607
- First thing we’ve got to do is
find out where she’s at.

1988
01:14:03,673 --> 01:14:05,208
- But how?

1989
01:14:05,275 --> 01:14:07,177
- We better see her
before she sees us,

1990
01:14:07,243 --> 01:14:08,478
because she’ll kill us.

1991
01:14:08,545 --> 01:14:09,847
- Just like that?

1992
01:14:09,913 --> 01:14:13,483
Well, I guess the first thing is
to find their trail.

1993
01:14:13,550 --> 01:14:15,385
- Well, she left
her curling iron.

1994
01:14:15,452 --> 01:14:17,653
She’ll be back,
and we’ll be ready for her.

1995
01:14:19,523 --> 01:14:21,825
- [ quacking ]

1996
01:14:23,693 --> 01:14:26,197
- Beverly! Beverla-ha-ha!

1997
01:14:26,263 --> 01:14:27,297
Oh, I love that one.

1998
01:14:28,765 --> 01:14:31,668
- Wait a minute, this tree
wasn’t here before.

1999
01:14:31,735 --> 01:14:32,668
- [ whispers ] Josie.

2000
01:14:32,735 --> 01:14:36,540
[ all whispering ]

2001
01:14:36,607 --> 01:14:37,540
- Shh! Shh!

2002
01:14:37,607 --> 01:14:39,042
- You can see
where they went.

2003
01:14:39,108 --> 01:14:40,510
- She probably held
a gun on him.

2004
01:14:40,577 --> 01:14:41,978
- You can tell a lot
from a leaf.

2005
01:14:42,045 --> 01:14:43,380
- Remember, I told you
she wasn't no good.

2006
01:14:43,447 --> 01:14:45,315
- It wasn’t exactly
a surprise to me.

2007
01:14:45,382 --> 01:14:48,352
Look, if she went through
this mess, I guess we can, too.

2008
01:14:48,418 --> 01:14:51,153
Now, remember, if she sees us,
we’re dead, so keep it quiet.

2009
01:14:51,222 --> 01:14:52,455
- What if we see her?

2010
01:14:52,522 --> 01:14:53,890
- What are we going to do
when we find her?

2011
01:14:53,957 --> 01:14:54,992
- Well, it beats me.

2012
01:14:55,058 --> 01:14:56,293
- Well,
then why do we have to...

2013
01:14:56,360 --> 01:14:59,062
- Oh, let’s do one thing
at a time. Come on.

2014
01:14:59,128 --> 01:15:00,897
- Hey, don’t push!
Don't push!

2015
01:15:00,963 --> 01:15:02,098
- Don’t you push me!

2016
01:15:02,165 --> 01:15:03,767
- Just keep quiet.

2017
01:15:03,833 --> 01:15:05,102
- Adirondack chairs.

2018
01:15:05,168 --> 01:15:07,938
- Oh, the un-cola man
should be sitting there.

2019
01:15:08,005 --> 01:15:10,673
- Wait, there's traces
of Groom & Clean on this bush.

2020
01:15:13,310 --> 01:15:16,112
- Maybe we should split up
into groups of one.

2021
01:15:16,145 --> 01:15:17,747
Let’s synchronize
your watch.

2022
01:15:23,453 --> 01:15:25,722
[ dramatic music ]

2023
01:15:25,788 --> 01:15:28,792
[ humming along ]

2024
01:15:30,060 --> 01:15:31,662
- Well, at least I look hot.

2025
01:15:31,728 --> 01:15:34,063
- You’re real dishy,
you know that?

2026
01:15:34,130 --> 01:15:36,500
- How long do we play
this game?

2027
01:15:36,567 --> 01:15:38,035
- Until it’s over.

2028
01:15:38,102 --> 01:15:39,035
- Oh.

2029
01:15:39,102 --> 01:15:40,637
- Behind here.

2030
01:15:40,703 --> 01:15:42,572
- I got a way to get us
in there,

2031
01:15:42,638 --> 01:15:43,940
and you’re going to lead us.

2032
01:15:44,007 --> 01:15:45,808
- How did she ever get up
in that tree?

2033
01:15:45,875 --> 01:15:47,343
- She’s going to catapult.

2034
01:15:47,410 --> 01:15:49,780
- How did she ever get up there
with all those guns?

2035
01:15:49,847 --> 01:15:51,682
- If I know Vera,
she's got them lined up

2036
01:15:51,748 --> 01:15:53,150
like a shooting gallery.

2037
01:15:53,217 --> 01:15:54,483
- Looks like Bob’s okay.

2038
01:15:54,550 --> 01:15:56,753
- I bet she’s got sandwiches
up there, too.

2039
01:15:56,820 --> 01:15:59,255
- We could spread out and flush
her from three sides.

2040
01:15:59,322 --> 01:16:01,358
- Exactly what she expects
us to do.

2041
01:16:01,425 --> 01:16:03,160
- Is she a good shot?

2042
01:16:03,227 --> 01:16:05,862
- She can hit anything
she can see.

2043
01:16:05,928 --> 01:16:07,297
If we were to rush out there,

2044
01:16:07,363 --> 01:16:08,932
we’d all three be dead
before we could reach her.

2045
01:16:08,998 --> 01:16:12,168
- Looks kind of like
Jane Russell in The Outlaw.

2046
01:16:12,235 --> 01:16:13,337
- Mm-hmm.

2047
01:16:13,403 --> 01:16:14,403
- What are we going to do?

2048
01:16:14,470 --> 01:16:16,407
- Impose sanctions.

2049
01:16:16,473 --> 01:16:18,975
- Now, she figures
that she can shoot us,

2050
01:16:19,042 --> 01:16:20,210
but we can’t shoot her.

2051
01:16:20,277 --> 01:16:21,445
- And that’s bad
for us, right?

2052
01:16:21,512 --> 01:16:23,380
- We’ve got nothing
to shoot her with.

2053
01:16:23,447 --> 01:16:25,015
- That's right,
so if we could shoot her,

2054
01:16:25,082 --> 01:16:26,683
the surprise would be
on our side.

2055
01:16:26,750 --> 01:16:28,885
- Yeah, that’d be
a real surprise, all right.

2056
01:16:28,952 --> 01:16:30,587
- Come on, I got an idea.

2057
01:16:30,653 --> 01:16:31,888
- Angels,
you're going undercover

2058
01:16:31,955 --> 01:16:33,657
at the swimsuit competition.

2059
01:16:35,092 --> 01:16:36,258
- What was our plan?

2060
01:16:36,327 --> 01:16:37,627
I’m all confused.

2061
01:16:37,693 --> 01:16:40,030
- I used to make these
when I was a kid.

2062
01:16:40,097 --> 01:16:41,932
Got a couple of rats
with them once.

2063
01:16:41,998 --> 01:16:43,167
- Weird childhood.

2064
01:16:43,233 --> 01:16:44,868
- Sure hope you can get
one more.

2065
01:16:44,935 --> 01:16:46,903
- How far do you think
you can throw it?

2066
01:16:46,970 --> 01:16:50,040
- I’m not exactly
the smallest girl in the class.

2067
01:16:50,107 --> 01:16:51,508
- Wow, what a range.

2068
01:16:51,542 --> 01:16:52,642
- But no trajectory.

2069
01:16:52,675 --> 01:16:53,777
- You two girls
circle around,

2070
01:16:53,843 --> 01:16:55,878
and then when I whistle
like I told you,

2071
01:16:55,945 --> 01:16:57,013
get her to take a shot
at you.

2072
01:16:57,080 --> 01:16:58,282
You got to get her to take
a shot at you,

2073
01:16:58,348 --> 01:17:00,017
but don’t do it so good
you get yourself killed.

2074
01:17:00,083 --> 01:17:02,987
- Uh, what risk
are you taking again?

2075
01:17:03,053 --> 01:17:04,855
- I sure hope you can throw
that thing.

2076
01:17:04,922 --> 01:17:06,323
- I do, too.
Now go on.

2077
01:17:06,390 --> 01:17:09,125
- So now Eve Arden’s in charge.

2078
01:17:09,192 --> 01:17:11,193
- You know, I bet they
probably missed the curfew

2079
01:17:11,260 --> 01:17:12,262
at the prison already.

2080
01:17:12,328 --> 01:17:13,797
- Yeah.

2081
01:17:13,863 --> 01:17:15,065
- This is Curt Gowdy.

2082
01:17:15,132 --> 01:17:17,100
Join me, Touch Conners,
and Eve Arden

2083
01:17:17,167 --> 01:17:20,903
as we hunt for Beverly Garland
on the Louisiana bayou.

2084
01:17:20,970 --> 01:17:22,138
Hello?

2085
01:17:23,340 --> 01:17:25,142
- Hootie hoo, hootie hoo!

2086
01:17:27,877 --> 01:17:29,078
- Hey, Vera!

2087
01:17:29,145 --> 01:17:30,113
- Oh, hi!

2088
01:17:30,180 --> 01:17:32,048
[ gunshots ]

2089
01:17:32,115 --> 01:17:33,717
- What, are the bullets
going to fall on her?

2090
01:17:34,785 --> 01:17:35,952
- Whoa! Hot!

2091
01:17:36,018 --> 01:17:37,353
Whoa! Stingy!

2092
01:17:42,325 --> 01:17:43,627
- Hey, Vera!

2093
01:17:43,693 --> 01:17:45,995
- I just want to know if
you have any cream rinse left!

2094
01:17:47,997 --> 01:17:49,065
- She caught it.

2095
01:17:51,300 --> 01:17:53,037
[ gunshot ]

2096
01:17:56,840 --> 01:17:58,175
[ gunshot ]

2097
01:17:59,843 --> 01:18:01,678
- Oh!
Think I would have learned.

2098
01:18:02,845 --> 01:18:04,580
- Top of the tree, Ma!

2099
01:18:04,647 --> 01:18:05,682
- Why don’t they come out?

2100
01:18:07,650 --> 01:18:10,687
- I don’t know,
kind of weird, isn’t it?

2101
01:18:16,693 --> 01:18:18,728
- Branch coming.

2102
01:18:18,795 --> 01:18:19,997
[ snake rattling ]

2103
01:18:20,063 --> 01:18:21,263
- Uh-oh!

2104
01:18:21,330 --> 01:18:23,167
- Oh ah! Here!

2105
01:18:28,572 --> 01:18:30,507
[ snake rattling ]

2106
01:18:34,710 --> 01:18:36,178
- Hey, hey,
what are you doing?

2107
01:18:38,382 --> 01:18:39,983
- Wait a minute,
she tied him to a tree

2108
01:18:40,050 --> 01:18:41,150
he can pull out of the ground?

2109
01:18:41,217 --> 01:18:43,320
- Is that the tree she’s in?

2110
01:18:43,387 --> 01:18:45,955
- Hey, Snake Conners.
- Mm-hmm.

2111
01:18:53,097 --> 01:18:54,030
- Oh!

2112
01:18:54,097 --> 01:18:56,533
- Oh, good catch, Beverly.

2113
01:18:56,600 --> 01:18:57,833
- Oh!

2114
01:18:57,900 --> 01:18:59,268
That was worse than the gun.

2115
01:18:59,302 --> 01:19:01,605
- There goes bikini season
for me.

2116
01:19:05,542 --> 01:19:06,677
- Hoo-ah!

2117
01:19:09,712 --> 01:19:11,047
- [ gunshot ]
- Oh!

2118
01:19:11,113 --> 01:19:12,715
- Hey, he was
just a Mannix fan.

2119
01:19:12,782 --> 01:19:14,517
He wanted his autograph.

2120
01:19:17,553 --> 01:19:20,790
- Off the 3-meter board,
Beverly Garland!

2121
01:19:20,857 --> 01:19:22,092
- I got her!
Come on!

2122
01:19:22,158 --> 01:19:24,627
- Now we got
to field dress her.

2123
01:19:24,693 --> 01:19:25,762
- She’s dead.

2124
01:19:25,828 --> 01:19:26,797
- Jim.

2125
01:19:26,863 --> 01:19:27,797
- Are you okay?

2126
01:19:27,863 --> 01:19:28,965
- Lot better than I was.

2127
01:19:29,032 --> 01:19:30,600
- She’s dead all right,
real dead.

2128
01:19:30,667 --> 01:19:33,068
- Wow, those two
look like kabuki actresses.

2129
01:19:33,137 --> 01:19:34,637
- That snake almost got you.

2130
01:19:34,703 --> 01:19:36,238
- Aah!
- Aah!

2131
01:19:36,305 --> 01:19:38,542
- If there’s one thing
I can’t stand it’s snakes.

2132
01:19:38,608 --> 01:19:39,910
Can’t you get rid of it?

2133
01:19:39,977 --> 01:19:42,645
- I didn’t care much
for this one, either.

2134
01:19:42,712 --> 01:19:44,613
Another second,
and I’d have been dead.

2135
01:19:44,680 --> 01:19:46,650
- She shot it?
- Yeah.

2136
01:19:46,717 --> 01:19:48,083
- Before the spear got her?

2137
01:19:48,152 --> 01:19:49,718
- No, afterwards.

2138
01:19:49,785 --> 01:19:51,722
Last thing
she did before she fell.

2139
01:19:51,788 --> 01:19:54,523
- Redemption, ladies and
gentlemen. Redemption.

2140
01:19:54,590 --> 01:19:56,827
- Funny thing,
she always wanted to kill.

2141
01:19:56,893 --> 01:19:58,127
Kill anything,

2142
01:19:58,195 --> 01:20:00,663
and the last thing she did
was save his life.

2143
01:20:00,730 --> 01:20:03,533
- The last thing she did was
kill a snake.

2144
01:20:03,567 --> 01:20:05,902
- You don’t need Andrea Dworkin
to figure that one out.

2145
01:20:05,968 --> 01:20:07,037
- Oh.

2146
01:20:07,103 --> 01:20:08,705
[ outboard motor starts ]

2147
01:20:08,772 --> 01:20:10,073
- Well, we’re back on track.

2148
01:20:10,140 --> 01:20:12,908
We lost another one
at that campsite.

2149
01:20:17,913 --> 01:20:20,617
- And as we re-entered
the clam flowage--

2150
01:20:20,683 --> 01:20:22,418
- Would you please?

2151
01:20:22,485 --> 01:20:25,022
So this gun was actually
in Betty Lou’s handbag?

2152
01:20:25,088 --> 01:20:26,857
- Would you please?

2153
01:20:29,058 --> 01:20:32,762
- Okay, we need volunteers
to get killed at this campsite.

2154
01:20:34,030 --> 01:20:35,832
- How much further
we got to go now, Josie?

2155
01:20:35,898 --> 01:20:37,067
- Just a couple of more miles.

2156
01:20:37,133 --> 01:20:39,068
- Oh, let’s go.

2157
01:20:39,135 --> 01:20:40,403
We're not taking any chances.

2158
01:20:40,470 --> 01:20:41,605
They’re probably waiting
for us.

2159
01:20:41,672 --> 01:20:42,905
It's going to get dark
pretty soon.

2160
01:20:42,972 --> 01:20:44,440
I want to see
when I get out of here.

2161
01:20:44,507 --> 01:20:45,742
Come on, now.

2162
01:20:45,808 --> 01:20:48,378
- Please, call me Touch.

2163
01:20:48,445 --> 01:20:51,113
- I’m not interested
in how you lost those girls.

2164
01:20:51,180 --> 01:20:52,515
I’m only interested
in finding them again.

2165
01:20:52,582 --> 01:20:54,952
- I know I haven’t been
in the film for a while.

2166
01:20:55,018 --> 01:20:57,153
- The slightest suspicion
and they'd just as soon

2167
01:20:57,220 --> 01:20:58,988
kill Lieutenant Hampton
as look at her.

2168
01:20:59,055 --> 01:21:00,757
- $2.00 for the first minute?
I understand.

2169
01:21:00,823 --> 01:21:02,792
- It doesn't matter now
whether we’re seen or not.

2170
01:21:02,858 --> 01:21:05,428
The important thing is
to make contact.

2171
01:21:05,495 --> 01:21:06,630
Sure, it's a big jungle,

2172
01:21:06,697 --> 01:21:07,997
but we’ve got
a big force out there.

2173
01:21:08,063 --> 01:21:10,633
- Yeah, apparently they brought
their evil in there.

2174
01:21:10,700 --> 01:21:12,402
- All right.

2175
01:21:12,468 --> 01:21:15,038
Dick, come in here,
will you?

2176
01:21:15,105 --> 01:21:17,440
- 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8,
20, 40, 50 million.

2177
01:21:17,507 --> 01:21:20,077
[ giggling ]

2178
01:21:20,143 --> 01:21:22,078
- I can hardly wait to get
to that fence

2179
01:21:22,145 --> 01:21:24,513
and turn these diamonds
into spending money.

2180
01:21:24,580 --> 01:21:27,083
- Cleaning your gun
with nail polish remover.

2181
01:21:27,150 --> 01:21:30,120
- How much is the cut three ways
now, huh, Josie?

2182
01:21:30,187 --> 01:21:33,188
- Seems to me you’d like to get
to that fence, too, Lee.

2183
01:21:33,257 --> 01:21:34,223
- Huh?

2184
01:21:34,290 --> 01:21:35,392
- Huh?

2185
01:21:35,458 --> 01:21:37,160
- Oh, I, uh...
I got one of my own.

2186
01:21:37,227 --> 01:21:38,628
- We grew up together.

2187
01:21:40,763 --> 01:21:43,132
- Well, maybe he could give me
a better price.

2188
01:21:43,198 --> 01:21:45,035
- Boy, she looks
like Vince Edwards.

2189
01:21:45,102 --> 01:21:47,503
- Well, I guess they all pay
about the same.

2190
01:21:47,570 --> 01:21:49,472
- You never know.

2191
01:21:49,538 --> 01:21:51,608
How would I get
in touch with him?

2192
01:21:51,675 --> 01:21:53,877
- I’d rather keep that
to myself.

2193
01:21:53,943 --> 01:21:56,847
- Well, that’s a fine way to act
after all we’ve done for you.

2194
01:21:56,913 --> 01:21:58,848
- It hasn’t been
a one-way street, you know.

2195
01:21:58,915 --> 01:21:59,950
- No, it’s been
more like a parkway.

2196
01:22:00,017 --> 01:22:01,150
- Yeah, that’s right.

2197
01:22:01,217 --> 01:22:02,285
- Well, I don’t think it’s
very...

2198
01:22:02,352 --> 01:22:04,153
- Forget it, Billie.

2199
01:22:04,220 --> 01:22:06,055
We should be out of here
in a couple of hours.

2200
01:22:06,122 --> 01:22:07,423
- The movie?

2201
01:22:07,490 --> 01:22:09,125
- It's sure going
to seem funny

2202
01:22:09,192 --> 01:22:11,227
without you ordering me
around, Josie.

2203
01:22:11,293 --> 01:22:13,262
- Going to seem funny
without you and Vera squabbling

2204
01:22:13,330 --> 01:22:14,797
all the time, too.

2205
01:22:14,863 --> 01:22:17,233
- Boy, women convicts are
a lot more supportive.

2206
01:22:17,300 --> 01:22:18,702
- Sure will.

2207
01:22:20,237 --> 01:22:22,338
[ distant engine ]

2208
01:22:22,405 --> 01:22:24,273
- Oh, my ride’s here. Bye.

2209
01:22:25,708 --> 01:22:28,378
- Expecting something?

2210
01:22:28,445 --> 01:22:29,945
- Oh, it’s just
my police backup. Doh!

2211
01:22:30,013 --> 01:22:31,280
- Aren’t you?

2212
01:22:31,347 --> 01:22:33,450
They probably got this whole
jungle surrounded.

2213
01:22:33,517 --> 01:22:35,518
- So it’s a jungle
or a swamp?

2214
01:22:35,585 --> 01:22:36,720
- I don’t know.

2215
01:22:36,787 --> 01:22:37,987
- Poor old Vera.

2216
01:22:38,053 --> 01:22:40,157
- She should have let
that snake get Bob.

2217
01:22:40,223 --> 01:22:41,825
- What do you mean?

2218
01:22:41,892 --> 01:22:43,225
- Save us the trouble.

2219
01:22:43,327 --> 01:22:44,693
- Aw, Josie.

2220
01:22:44,760 --> 01:22:46,195
Can’t you think
of no other way?

2221
01:22:46,262 --> 01:22:47,730
He’s cute.

2222
01:22:47,797 --> 01:22:49,565
- He may be cute,
but as long as he can talk,

2223
01:22:49,632 --> 01:22:51,367
we got a couple
extra murder raps.

2224
01:22:51,433 --> 01:22:52,635
- If you got one,
you got a dozen.

2225
01:22:52,702 --> 01:22:54,670
- Why don’t you just tie him up
and leave him?

2226
01:22:54,737 --> 01:22:55,838
- Why should we?

2227
01:22:55,905 --> 01:22:58,475
- Uh, what are you guys
talking about?

2228
01:22:58,542 --> 01:23:00,043
- We’re close to the edge
of the jungle.

2229
01:23:00,110 --> 01:23:02,478
A gunshot will bring whoever’s
looking for us a-runnin'.

2230
01:23:02,545 --> 01:23:03,813
- So what’s my subtext here?

2231
01:23:03,880 --> 01:23:05,015
- What makes you so sure
somebody’s looking for us?

